{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '120,260p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && cat vendor/engine/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md\"","aggregated_output":"```js full-script\ngame.script(function* () {\n  yield 1;                                   // seconds of game time\n  yield E.until(() => door.open);            // a condition\n  yield game.tween(boss, { y: 80 }, 1.5);    // a tween (or another script, or a generator) finishing\n  for (let w = 0; w < 3; w++) { spawnWave(w); yield E.any([8, () => enemies.length === 0]); }\n});\n```\n  `E.all([...])` waits for all; a bare `yield` waits one step. It runs at once to its first `yield`, the same at any refresh rate; `{ keep: true }` outlives the scene; `.cancel()`, `.done`, `.value`.\n- Paths: `const p = new E.Path([[x, y, z], ...], { closed, smooth: 'catmull' })`: `p.length`, `p.at(d)` (`{ x, y, z, angle }` by distance along: moving platforms, dives, rails), `p.nearest(x, y)` (a racer's progress), `p.draw(r)` to see it.\n- Weather: `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' | 'snow' | 'ash' | 'leaves' | 'sand', amount: .8, wind: .3, lightning: .2 }` (null: clear) falls through the world in every view, settles or splashes, flashes and thunders; cosmetic only (its own random stream), and it ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n- Wrap-around (Asteroids): `x = E.wrap(x, 0, W)`, `E.wrapDiff(a, b, W)` (the short way across the seam), and `wrap: [W, H]` on `r.sprite` or `r.actor` draws a copy across each edge.\n\n## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\nWith no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter, the frame rate and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim and move, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen, the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\n- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`, `touch: 'never'` (a phone is told a controller or keyboard is needed). `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\n- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | 'load')` opens the screen from your own menu. Blocked storage keeps them for the visit.\n- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }]` (a standard key without a label sets its default). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('settings')`. From code: `game.settings.set(key, v)`, `game.fullscreen.toggle()` (from a key, click or tap), `game.pause(reason)`, `game.resume()`. `live: true` (or `game.menu(name, { pause: false })`): menus over a world that keeps stepping (online play).\n- **Boot**: heavy setup in steps behind a boot screen, and a report for any error before play: `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title, steps: [['Building the city', () => { map = build(); }]] } })` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Boot).\n\n## Input: `game.input`\n- Actions in every preset: `up down left right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad), `start` (Enter, Start), `pause` (Escape, P, Start), `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z, pad A), `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B).\n- DEFAULT adds `attack` (J, X, click), `dash` (Space, Shift, K), `skill` (L, E, right click), `jump` (Z). PLATFORMER: `jump` (Space, Z, K, pad A), `attack` (X, J, click), `dash` (Shift, C, L), `skill`. SHMUP: `fire` (Space, Z, J, click), `bomb` (X, K). THIRDPERSON: `sprint` (Shift), `jump` (Space), `crouch` (C, Ctrl), `interact` (E, F), `attack` (J), `block` (K), `dodge` (L), `use` (Q), `map` (M, Tab).\n- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPressed()`, `move()` (screen direction `[x, y]`, length up to 1), `use(preset)`, `touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'])`, `touchSet('confirm', 'TALK', near)` (a context button: relabel it, or hide it while it has nothing to do).\n- Moves: `input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing })` is true on the step a quarter circle forward and punch ends (numpad notation, mirrored when `facing` is -1: `'623'`, `'41236'`); `input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down+right', 'attack'], { window: .5 })` any run of inputs (a cheat code); `input.history` the last second of them (`{ t, dir, pressed }`, for an input display).\n- Players (two to four on one machine): `game.players` is `[game.input, ...]`, each an input with this API, its `player` number, `name` (`'P2'`), `color` (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and device. `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin: (input, n) => {} })` lets them in: Start on a free gamepad, or 2 on the keyboard (player 2 takes its right half: arrows, `.` `/` `,` and the numpad; player 1 keeps WASD with F G H; a preset's `halves: { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: {...} }` its own); `game.addPlayer({ pad: 0 })` or `({ keys: 'right' })`, `game.removePlayer(p)`. Prompts, the pause (P2 PAUSED), a lost controller and the Controls screen are per player. One screen: `cam.frame(heroes)`. Split: `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [h1, h2], layout: 'auto' })` (`'columns'`, `'rows'`, `'grid'`; up to 4) draws the scene once per viewport (`r.viewport` is `{ i, x, y, w, h }`), then `scene.hud(r)` once over the whole screen; `game.viewports[i].follow(t)` or `.focus(x, y)`.\n- `clear()` releases held inputs, pending presses, virtual sticks and touch buttons; focus loss does this automatically. `suppress(a)` blocks an action for the current tick; `suppressCode('Mouse0')` lets a HUD widget consume that mouse button while other devices bound to the action still work.\n- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same; the right stick is `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right`, the wheel `WheelUp`/`WheelDown`; `value(a)`: 0 to 1 (a trigger's travel, a stick's push). Options while Create is held is no press (the AI Hub's chord).\n- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch buttons cover the screen (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, or null): keep a prompt clear of it. `clicked()`: where a click or tap on the canvas landed (`[x, y]` in screen pixels) the step after it, else null; `pointer()`: the mouse in screen pixels; `drag()`: how far the stick's finger moved this step (`[dx, dy]`, or null), to steer one to one; `steer = 'drag'`: a finger anywhere steers, no stick drawn (`stickOn`: a finger is on it). `zones = [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }]` (fractions of the canvas): a finger in one holds its act until it lifts (a pinball's halves). Gestures (a mouse or one finger, screen pixels): `box()` → `{ x0, y0, x1, y1, done }` (a left drag; on touch a long press, then a drag), `longPress()`, `doubleTap()`, `pan()` → `[dx, dy]` (a finger's drag on open ground, a middle or right drag), `zoomPoint()`; `feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch, button, id })` plays a pointer in a test. `bindButtons(root)` wires `[data-act]` elements.\n\n## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n- Background: `r.sky(['#top', '#mid', '#bottom'])`, `r.starfield({ count, speed, dir: 'down' | 'left' })`.\n- Depth sorted: `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: '#ffffff', flashMix: .75, alpha, xray, outline, ghost, emissive, every, key })` (the flash tints over the sprite so shading shows: `flashMix` .5 by default, 1 solid; `every: 2, key: npc` redraws a background character every other frame; actors up to about 250 px tall), `r.sprite(x, y, z, sprite, { flip, anchor: 'bottom' | 'center', glow, flash })`, `r.queue(x, y, z, g => {...}, { bias })` (sorted by that one point: a long wall by `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn)`), `r.actorNow(...)` (as `r.actor`, drawn at once over what is drawn so far), `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)` (inside a queue function). `{ pick: unit }` on any of them (and `r.shape`), then `r.pick(sx, sy)` → what the last frame drew under a screen point, front to back.\n- Floor marks: `r.shadow(x, y, radius, alpha, color, surfaceZ)`, `r.decal(g => r.groundArc(...))`, `r.groundDisc`, `r.groundRing`, `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n, z)`.\n- On top, unlit, screen pixels: `r.text(str, x, y, color, { align, scale, outline })`, `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color)`, `r.overlay(g => {...})`.\n- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case: ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, the accented Latin letters; any other is `?`; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars })` (`voice`: a sound, or `(ch, i, talk) => {}` per letter); `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value from `say(text, { vars })` or `talk.vars`.\n- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse over one moves the cursor. A tap on a dialog box turns its page as confirm does.\n- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(title, text)`.\n\n## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (ice .15), `carry` (a conveyor), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` and `respawn` (`level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` (a grapple: a pendulum, jump lets go); draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors. State: `crouching`, `hanging`, `clinging`, `swimming`, `onRope`, `onBars`, `swinging`, `rolling`; `rigState()` poses them.\n- Moving platforms: `{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }` boxes you move yourself and pass as `solids`; riders are carried.\n\n**Body** (top-down / isometric / brawler): `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, friction: 0, bounce: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Set `vx`, `vy`, then `body.update(dt, map)`. Also `push(ix, iy, iz)` (knockback), `jump(v)`, and `onGround`, `z`, `groundZ`, `hitWall`, `landed`, `bounced` (hit the ground and bounced: dust, a thud). Walls lower than your feet are walkable, so bodies can jump onto blocks.\n\n**Mover** (third person): `const mover = new E.Mover({ x, y })`; `mover.update(dt, map, game.input)` (input `'THIRDPERSON'`) or an AI's `{ move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }`: it sprints, sneaks, climbs, vaults, leaps gaps, hops down and rolls; `climbAny: true` climbs any wall (jump at it; up the screen is up the wall; jump leaps up, crouch lets go; `mover.wall`, `map.wall(from, dir)`), `glide: true` glides (jump again in the air; `lift`: an updraft), `staminaMax: 100` (climbing, gliding and sprinting spend `mover.stamina`); `rig.update(dt, mover.rigState())`; `mover.play('takedown', { other })`, your own `E.ACTIONS`. Stealth: `E.sees(guard, hero, { map })` → `{ seen, exposure }`, `E.hears`, `new E.Suspicion()` (`update(dt, seen, hero)` → `'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'`), `r.sightCone(guard, { map })`, `r.marker(x, y, z, { label })`.\n\n**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover }`. `if (input.buffered('attack') && slash.start()) input.consume('attack')`; `slash.update(dt)` (returns the phase that just began); `slash.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 22, 1.4), e => {...})` hits each target once per swing during `'active'` (moves wait until `hitAt: .35` of the swing, so hit-stop freezes the strike, not the wind-up); `rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: slash.state })`. Also `busy`, `active`, `cancel()`. **Combo**: `const combo = new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut'], { window: .3 })` (names, specs or Attacks); `combo.press()` starts or chains the next hit; `update`, `hits`, `state`, `step` work the same. **Knockback**: `E.knockback(attacker, target, 160, up)` pushes a Body (or anything with vx / vy) away.\n\n**Bullets**: `const shots = new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side' })`; `shots.fire({ x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r: 2, team: 'player', color, life, dmg, pierce, sprite })`; `shots.burst(base, E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed))`; `shots.update(dt, map)`; `shots.hit(targets, (b, t) => {...}, 'player')`; `shots.draw(r)`; `shots.clear(team)`. Patterns: `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`, `aim(a, b, speed)`, `aimSide(a, b, speed)`, `spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`, `ring(n, speed, offset)`. In side view the second number of a pattern velocity is vz.\n\n**Helpers**: `E.dist(a, b)`, `E.angleTo(a, b)`, `E.arc(a, b, gravity, { apex | time | speed })` → `{ vx, vy, vz, t }` (a throw that lands at b: a lob, a grenade), `E.overlap(a, b)` (circles x, y, r), `E.overlapBox(a, b)` (side boxes x center, z feet, w, h), `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)` (melee cone; `dz` limits the height difference), `E.rand(a, b)`, `E.randInt(a, b)`, `E.pick(list)`, `E.chance(p)`, `E.prune(list, fn)`, `E.store.get(key, fallback)` / `set(key, value)` (save data; slots: `game.saves`), `new E.SpatialHash(32)` (`build(list)`, `near(x, y, r, fn)`), `new E.FlowField(map)` (`update(tx, ty)` or `update([[x, y], ...])`: the nearest; `dir(x, y, tx, ty)` walks around walls and `map.solid` shapes), math `clamp lerp approach ease.* angDiff approachAng smoothDamp rng(seed) noise2 hex shade mix`; `E.version` (the release) and `E.versionLabel()` ('v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': show it on a title or a debug screen).\n\n## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists) | a game's own (`E.Humanoid.weapon(id, { length, rest, draw(w) })`; `.hat(id, draw)`, `.pose(id, (J, w) => ...)`; `draw: { under, over }`; state `tilt`, `roll`), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat. `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above the feet), `flip: 0..1` (a roll), `land: k` (a heavy landing); `mover.rigState()` sets them. Every wind-up starts from the rig's current pose, so chained hits and hand changes never snap. Idle rigs breathe and shift their weight by themselves.\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's build order and waves; `cam.free`, `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick`, buildings as `E.SHAPES`, E.Shell's minimap; bodies drawn `every: 3` | RTS |\n| Theme park or city sim (Theme Park, RollerCoaster Tycoon, SimCity) | `iso` | paths as floor tags walked on an `E.Grid`, agents with `E.needs` picking by `E.choose`, `E.Clock` days and light, `game.timeScale` 0 to 4, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`; rides as shapes stepped through angles (`params`, `facing`) | SIM |\n| 3D platformer or adventure remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash) | `iso` / `threequarter` / `brawler` | TileMap blocks of different heights + Body `jump()` (z is real height); in real 3D: `E.World3D` (the 3D engine's manual), `camera.lock` | ADVENTURE; 3D ACTION, 3D PLATFORMER |\n| Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark) | the 3D engine's `'zones'` camera | `camera.zones` (fixed cameras by room), `camera.steer` (tank controls), `camera.lock` to aim, `world.through` doors, `world.flashlight`, fog; `E.RPG` inventory, `game.saves` | 3D HORROR |\n| First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) | the 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes | cells of 2 x 2 tiles stepped and turned a quarter at a time (tweened), `E.Grid` paths for the monsters, `E.Turns` `'atb'` (real time) or `'speed'` (turns), `E.Fog` for the automap, `world.thing('door')` gates and `world.unlock`, `rig.drawPortrait` for the party | 3D CRAWLER |\n| Rhythm (Dance Dance Revolution, PaRappa, Beatmania, Space Channel 5) | any (a highway on the overlay) | `E.Rhythm` (the rhythm module): a chart of lane strings in parts on a song's steps, judged in ms of the music clock, combo, life, grade, holds, calls a teacher plays and you answer, `rh.draw` (`arrows: true`); the songbook's songs (`E.Songbook`); lanes as `input.zones` on a phone; `audio.onBeat` moves the dancer | RHYTHM |\n| Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam) | `threequarter` / `topdown` | the ball an `E.Body` (`bounce`; curl: turn its velocity across its path), passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` for a lob, a shot's meter, formations by where the ball is, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` | SPORTS |\n| Third-person stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu) | `iso` / `threequarter` | TileMap roofs, Mover, `E.sees`, `E.Suspicion`, FlowField `jump` | STEALTH |\n| Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero) | Mode 7 (the mode7 module, over any view) | `E.Mode7` over a TileMap track (floor tags: grass, sand, boost), `E.Car` karts (`kart: true`: hop, drift, boost) in an `E.Race` round an `E.Path` (laps, checkpoints, drivers, items), rigs in karts as billboards, `game.splitScreen(2)` for two | KART |\n| 3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.track` (banked, walls, pads, `gaps` for a shortcut), `world.vehicle` karts raced by `E.Race`, split screen through `world.cameras` | 3D RACING |\n| Rail shooters (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.flyer` on rails or free in bounds, rolls (`f.rolling`) turn shots aside, `f.seek` for a charged lock, `Dialog`'s radio | 3D FLIGHT |\n| Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Road Rash) | the pseudo-3D road (the road module) | `E.Road` segments (curves, hills, tunnels), scenery and traffic placed on it, `curveAt` throwing the car outward, a clock and checkpoints | ROAD |\n| Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA) | `topdown` / `iso` | `E.Car` on a TileMap (its floor tags slow it, its walls bounce it), `E.Race` for laps and drivers, cars drawn with `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points | KART |\n| First-person shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007, Apex Legends) | the 3D engine's first person (or third) | a level of text rows or a terrain, `world.ray` hitscan, recoil and reloads, doors (`world.thing('door')`), raiders on `world.flow()` | 3D SHOOTER |\n| Bomberman, Frogger, Sokoban, Gauntlet, Robotron; Sonic, Prince of Persia; light guns | as the recipe says | `AI_GUIDE.md`'s Genre recipes: each on the kit closest to it | (a recipe) |\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |\n| speck, noise | amount .08; scale 4 | specks; soft patches |\n| foliage | size 3.5 | leaf clumps lit on top |\n| bark | | fissures; rings on a cut end |\n| metal | rivet | a shine where lit; rivets |\n| cloth | fold .9 | weave and folds |\n| glaze | | a glossy shine |\n| thatch, shingles | course; bw | straw courses; roof tiles |\n\nYour own pattern: `E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0` (s.u, s.v: world units\nacross and up the surface; s.lid, s.curved, s.lit, s.W, s.H; return a step, -1 to +2). A material may also paint one kind\nof surface its own way, per pixel: `face(wx, z, tones, type, cx, cy, fi, nh, h)` or `roof(wx, wy, tones, type)` returning\na color or null, `floor(x, y, tag, view)` returning [r, g, b].\n\n## Write one\n\nUnits: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. The origin is the middle of the footprint on the ground; write it\nfacing south (+y). Use whole or half units: a pixel at game size is about 0.7 units.\n\n```js\nE.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'round three-legged stool', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { w: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','l',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8],{rot:[0,-8,0]}]]] };\n```\n\nAn entry: `about`, `tags`, `mats` (slot to material; a slot name that is not in mats is a material itself), and `parts`, or\n`make(params)` returning parts with `params` its defaults. Optional: `scale` (times the placement's), `foot: [x0, y0,\nx1, y1]` (the footprint for collision, and for sorting when it stands raised; the bounds by default), `lights: [[x, y,\nz, color, radius]]`, `flames: [[x, y, z, w, h]]`.\n\n| Part | Form | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| box | `['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]` | at: the bottom middle |\n| cyl | `['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]` | r2: top radius (0: a cone); sq squashes y; seg: 6 for a hexagon |\n| lathe | `['lathe', m, at, [[r, z], ...], { seg }]` | a profile turned about z, bottom to top; [0, z] closes an end |\n| ball | `['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]` | at: its centre; sz below 1 flattens it |\n| prism | `['prism', m, at, [[a, b], ...], h, { axis }]` | an outline pushed h: up z (outline x, y), or centred along y (outline x, z) or x (outline y, z) |\n| wedge | `['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]` | h tall at the back, down to the floor at the front |\n| rock | `['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]` | a lumpy, faceted ball; below the floor is not drawn |\n| use | `['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]` | another shape inside this one |\n| mirror | `['mirror', 'x' \\| 'y' \\| 'xy', part]` | the part and its mirror copies |\n| ring, row | `['ring', n, radius, part]`, `['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]` | n copies round z (the part moved out to radius); n copies in a line, centred |\n| group | `['group', at, rot, [parts]]` | parts moved and turned together |\n\nEvery part takes `{ rot }`: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Write arrays densely (`[0,0,8]`, not `[0, 0, 8]`):\nspaces cost a third more tokens.\n\n### Worked entries\n\n```js\nbarrel: { about: 'oak barrel, two iron hoops', tags: 'container wood', mats: { w: 'oak', h: 'iron' },\n  parts: [['lathe','w',[0,0,0],[[0,0],[5,0],[6,3],[6.5,8],[6,13],[5,16],[0,16]]], ['row',2,[0,0,9],['cyl','h',[0,0,7.5],6.5,1.5]]] },\ncrate: { about: 'wooden crate, framed and braced', tags: 'container wood', mats: { c: 'crate' }, parts: [['box','c',[0,0,0],[15,15,14]]] },\ntable: { about: 'plank table, four legs', tags: 'furniture tavern', mats: { t: 'oak', l: 'walnut' },\n  parts: [['box','t',[0,0,10],[24,14,2]], ['mirror','xy',['box','l',[10,5,0],[2,2,10]]]] },\nchest: { about: 'oak chest, round lid, iron bands', tags: 'container treasure', mats: { w: 'oak', b: 'iron', l: 'gold' },\n  parts: [['box','w',[0,0,0],[16,10,8]], ['prism','w',[0,0,8],[[-5,0],[5,0],[4,3],[0,5],[-4,3]],16,{axis:'x'}],\n    ['mirror','x',['box','b',[5.5,0,0],[1.5,11,8.5]]], ['box','l',[0,5,5],[3,1,3]]] },\nlamppost: { about: 'iron street lamp, glowing head', tags: 'town light', mats: { m: 'iron', g: 'flame' }, lights: [[0,0,40,'#ffd070',70]],\n  parts: [['cyl','m',[0,0,0],2.5,3], ['cyl','m',[0,0,3],1,34], ['box','g',[0,0,37],[4,4,5]], ['cyl','m',[0,0,42],3.5,3,{r2:0,seg:4}]] },\nfence: { about: 'rail fence, len long (16)', tags: 'village farm', mats: { w: 'oak' }, params: { len: 16 },\n  make: p => [['mirror','x',['box','w',[p.len / 2 - 1,0,0],[2,2,12]]], ['row',2,[0,0,5],['box','w',[0,0,6],[p.len - 2,1,1.5]]]] },\n```\n\nA generator seeds its noise from its params (`E.rng(seed)`), never `Math.random`, so it draws the same pixels everywhere.\n\n## Make one: the recipe\n\n1. **Read this card whole.**\n2. **Find** the nearest entry: `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"` searches the core library and the store's sets\n   (`src/assets/sets/`, about a thousand objects, materials and sprites converted from CC0 libraries, each with where it\n   came from) and `--show set:id` prints one; the Asset Lab (`/asset-lab`) shows them all.\n3. **Copy** it and change its names, parts and materials, or write a new one from the parts above. Give the cue a player\n   knows it by parts of its own (a skep's coils as stacked rings, an anvil's horn, a barrow's open tub dark inside), and\n   keep small parts plain ('none', 'glaze'): a busy pattern on a part a few pixels wide reads as speckle.\n4. **Look:** `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` (a file that sets `E.SHAPES.stool`, or a store set; a core id\n   alone works too: `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs barrel`). It draws `check-output/asset-sheet/stool.png`: every view and\n   four facings, beside the hero, on a light and a dark floor. It lints what reads badly: too small from above, a part\n   under a pixel, too few tones, low contrast with the floor, its tokens. Read the picture, fix, repeat.\n5. **Use** it: `E.SHAPES.stool = {...}` and `r.shape('stool', ...)`; or a set file\n   (`(window.ASSETS = window.ASSETS || {}).MINE = { set: 'MINE', format: 1, materials, shapes }`) and\n   `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS.MINE)`, which names its entries 'MINE:stool' so they never collide, and returns the names.\n   A store set loads the same way (its script, then `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`);\n   `node tools/asset-set.mjs <sets> --ids a,b --name mine --out mine.js` cuts the few a game uses, with what they need\n   (Emberdeep's set dressing loads `src/assets/sets/emberdeep.js`, cut so).\n\n## Limits\n\n- Still objects. Lids that open, swinging signs and held weapons are code (or props) for now.\n- A shape sorts by one point, as props do; a long one (a bed, a cart) may cross a body walking right beside it.\n- Collision is the footprint's box, turned with the shape, and the bounds' height: a table is solid under its top too.\n- Bigger than about 240 pixels on screen, a shape skips the actors' effects (flash, x-ray).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The title is **K.C. Munchkin Mix-Up**. The engine and Hub revisions match the plan’s baselines. I verified the original moving-food rules and inspected footage; the core will use twelve fleeing snacks, three predators, and shortcuts that reward interception.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '96,119p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && sed -n '205,245p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && cat vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '96,119p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && sed -n '205,245p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/API.md && cat vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"- `views`: the views your game supports; `game.nextView()` cycles them (bind it to a key).\n- Start: `game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) })`, or with scenes (below).\n- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `hook('input' | 'step' | 'enter', fn)` (your own each step, paused too for input; returns its removal), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\n- Fields: `W`, `H` (screen pixels), `time`, `real`, `timeScale` (0.25 = slow motion), `paused`, `input`, `audio`, `particles`, `lights`, `view`, `errors`, `cam`. `game.fail('my power', err)` reports an error in your code (logged, in `errors`, on the error panel) and plays on.\n- Camera zoom and turn: `game.setZoom(1.5)` (.5 .. 3; everything drawn by the engine re-rasterizes crisply, the HUD stays), `game.rotateView(45)` (ground views only), `game.resetCamera()` (to the scene's zoom), `game.zoom`, `game.yaw`, `game.note('ZOOM 2x')` (a short notice at the top of the screen; `game.shownNote` is the one showing). Custom painters can read `r.view.zoom` (undefined at 1x) to scale their own art.\n- The player's zoom: a scene's `camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5 }` lets the player zoom within `zoom` from `start` (wheel, `-` `=`, pinch, Settings; `false`: none; `AI_GUIDE.md`, Camera).\n- Tests and tools: `new E.Game({ headless: true })` (the default in Node: no screen, sound or DOM; `draw` is skipped, or with `draw: true` run on a stand-in, its errors in `game.errors`) or `{ loop: false }` runs only by `game.advance(seconds, { draw })` (exact fixed steps at once); `input.tap(action)` presses for one step, `input.hold(action, on)`; `game.debug = { snapshot() {...} }` is your game's handle (`tools/check.mjs` prints it); `game.stop()`, `start()`, `dispose()`.\n- Sessions: `?record=1`, then the pause menu's Save session; `node tools/replay.mjs session.json` replays it exactly, headless (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Sessions).\n- Camera: `cam.offset = [dx, dy]` sits the focus that many screen pixels from the centre (above a phone's touch buttons: `[0, -60]`); `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)` keeps it inside the level (in side views a level shorter than the screen sits on the bottom edge; `cam.align = 'center'` to change); `cam.room = [160, 128]` moves screen by screen (Zelda, Metroid) and `cam.moving` is true while it slides; `cam.smooth` = lag in seconds (0: locked to the target); `cam.window = [48, 24]` a dead zone the focus moves in before the camera follows; `cam.snapY = true` follows a followed body's height only when it lands (side-scrollers); `cam.frame([p1, p2], { margin, zoom: [.5, 1] })` keeps them all in view, zooming out as they part (`frame(null)` stops); `cam.free = { keys, edge: 10, drag, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }` a free camera (strategy, sims): keys, a stick, the screen's edge or a drag pan it, a zoom goes toward the pointer or the pinch.\n\n## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n```js\ngame.start({ scene: 'title', scenes: {\n  title: { update(dt) { if (game.input.pressed('start')) game.go('play', { level: 1 }); },\n           draw(r) { r.sky(['#101848', '#402a70']); r.text('PRESS START', r.W / 2, 100, '#fff', { align: 'center', scale: 2 }); } },\n  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n          enter(data) { /* build the level */ }, exit() {}, update(dt) {}, draw(r) {} }\n} });\n```\n`game.go(name, data)` switches after a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`: a test advances past it; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: .4, at: hero }` a transition, a plain fade under reduce motion); timers (but `after(s, fn, { keep: true })`) and particles are cleared, a hit-stop ends (`timeScale` stays). `pausable: true`: Escape / P / Start pauses it, with the pause menu (below). `view`, `views`, `input`, `res`, `expand`, `touch`, `camera`, `propSize` are options applied on entry (a method so named warns). A scene is one object every visit: reset its state in `enter`. `back()` takes a phone's back gesture first (true if it went back: a sub-menu closed).\n\n## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n- Tweens (Phaser's): `game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases numbers on game time: paused with the game, slowed by `timeScale`, ended by a scene change unless `keep`. Returns `{ done, cancel() }`. `E.ease` has Penner's set: `linear`, `inSine` `outSine` `inOutSine`, `inQuad` `outQuad` `inOutQuad`, the same for `Cubic`, `Back`, `Elastic`, `Bounce`.\n- Scripts (Unity's coroutines) for cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials:\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists) | a game's own (`E.Humanoid.weapon(id, { length, rest, draw(w) })`; `.hat(id, draw)`, `.pose(id, (J, w) => ...)`; `draw: { under, over }`; state `tilt`, `roll`), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat. `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above the feet), `flip: 0..1` (a roll), `land: k` (a heavy landing); `mover.rigState()` sets them. Every wind-up starts from the rig's current pose, so chained hits and hand changes never snap. Idle rigs breathe and shift their weight by themselves.\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n// The ARCADE kit's game (a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/32-arcade.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. arcade.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs arcade runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 10  ARCADE  (a cabinet of three golden-age classics: Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids). @modules arcade grid gen\n * Three short games, each a remaster (lit, with HD rigs, glowing lines and particles) with the classic look one key away\n * (C, a pad's Y, or Settings: Arcade, Look), each with its own high-score table, initials on a letter wheel, a continue,\n * two players taking turns, and a demo in the attract mode.\n *   MAZE (#arcade/maze): eat every glow-seed in a hedge maze while four wisps hunt you, each its own way (one chases, one\n *     heads you off, one flanks with the first, one is shy up close), in waves of scatter and chase; a lantern seed turns\n *     them blue and edible for a while; the side tunnel wraps round. Each maze is new (E.gen's braided maze, mirrored);\n *     an intermission after the first.\n *   FORMATION (#arcade/formation): moths fly in on curved paths (E.Path), form up and sway, then dive at you along paths\n *     of their own, turning as they fly (r.sprite's rot); two shots on screen at a time; a stage card between waves.\n *   ROCKS (#arcade/rocks): turn, thrust and drift through a field of rocks that split when shot; the screen's edges meet\n *     (E.wrap); a saucer hunts you; hyperspace when cornered. Glowing vector lines.\n * The cabinet (#arcade) is the title: left and right pick a game, up and down one or two players. Left alone it plays a\n * demo of each game in turn (its own bot), then shows that game's table. The sides of a wide screen show cabinet art\n * drawn by code. Keys: arrows / WASD, Space / Z / J fire (rocks: up thrusts, X / K hyperspace), Enter start, C classic.\n * TOUCH: the stick, FIRE (rocks: THRUST and WARP too); a tap picks a cabinet, and the letter wheel takes taps.\n * HOW IT WORKS: E.Arcade (the arcade module) keeps the scores, lives, turns, tables, initials, cards, the continue and the\n * attract mode; the maze is an E.Grid with E.GridMovers (a turn asked early is kept), each game a { begin, step, draw }.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst ARCADE = (() => {\n  const KEYS = Object.assign({}, E.Input.SHMUP, { thrust: ['Pad2', 'Pad5'], warp: ['KeyX', 'KeyK', 'ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1', 'Pad6'], classic: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'] });\n  delete KEYS.bomb;\n  game.settings.define({ key: 'arcadeLook', group: 'Arcade', label: 'Look', options: [['remaster', 'Remaster'], ['classic', 'Classic']], value: 'remaster', help: 'Remaster: lit, with HD rigs and glowing lines. Classic: as the cabinets first looked. C switches it in play' });\n  const classic = () => game.settings.arcadeLook === 'classic';\n  // the cabinet's own tune (the step sequencer's format): A minor, a bouncing bass\n  const SONG = { bpm: 132, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .12, notes: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 - G5 . E5 . C5 . D5 . | E5 - - . D5 . C5 . B4 . G4 . A4 - - . | F4 . A4 . C5 . F5 - E5 . C5 . A4 . B4 . | C5 . B4 . A4 . G#4 . A4 - - - - . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . | C3 . C4 . C3 . C4 . G2 . G3 . G2 . G3 . | F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . | E2 . E3 . E2 . E3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .12, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h' }] };\n  // the remaster's deep space (the classic look keeps plain black): a planet, nebulae drifting, many stars\n  const SPACE = [['#020208', '#0a0a24', '#1a0c30', '#2a1038'], ['#02040a', '#06142a', '#0c1c3a', '#1a1a3a']].map((sky, i) => new E.Backdrop({ sky, moon: { x: i ? .16 : .82, y: i ? .7 : .22, r: i ? 22 : 15, color: i ? '#8ab0d8' : '#b89ae8' }, stars: 140,\n    layers: [{ kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#1a4a6a' : '#6a3aa8', y: .3, height: .45, parallax: .03, drift: 1, nebula: true, seed: 2 + i }, { kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#3a2a5a' : '#2a5ab0', y: .72, height: .4, parallax: .05, drift: 2, nebula: true, seed: 5 + i }] }));\n  // cabinet art round a playfield of one fixed screen: on a wide screen's sides (left of x0, right of x1) a lit bezel edge,\n  // a marquee stripe and drifting sparks; on a tall one (above y0, below y1) the marquee with the game's name and the\n  // control panel\n  function cabinet(r, x0, x1, hue, y0 = 0, y1 = r.H, label = '') {\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      const H = r.H, t = game.time;\n      if (y0 > 40) {\n        px.rect(g, 0, 0, r.W, y0 - 4, '#0a0614'); px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 34, hue[0]); px.blend(g, .25, 'add', () => px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 12, '#ffffff'));\n        E.font.title(g, label, r.W / 2, y0 - 42, { align: 'center', scale: 2, colors: ['#ffffff', '#1a1030'], depth: 1 });\n      }\n      if (H - y1 > 40) {\n        const y = y1 + 6; px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, H - y, '#140c22'); px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, 2, hue[0]);\n        const cy = y + Math.min(40, (H - y) / 2); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy, 8, '#2a1a3e'); px.rect(g, r.W / 2 - 51, cy - 16, 3, 16, '#c8c8d0'); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy - 17, 5, '#ff4a4a');\n        for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.disc(g, r.W / 2 + 10 + i * 18, cy, 6, hue[i]);\n      }\n      for (const [a, b, right] of [[0, x0, false], [x1, r.W, true]]) {\n        if (b - a < 3) continue;\n        // the side's art: a dark panel tinted toward the game's colour, lit stripes slanting across it\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) px.rect(g, a, Math.floor(H * i / 8), b - a, Math.ceil(H / 8) + 1, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .03 + i * .018));\n        g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(a, 0, b - a, H); g.clip();\n        for (let x = a - H; x < b + 40; x += 46) { const k = right ? 1 : -1, x1 = right ? x : b - (x - a); px.blend(g, .1, 'add', () => px.poly(g, [[x1, 0], [x1 + 18 * k, 0], [x1 + 18 * k + H * .5 * k, H], [x1 + H * .5 * k, H]], hue[1])); }\n        const sw = (y0, y1, c) => px.poly(g, right ? [[a, H * y0], [b, H * (y0 - .3)], [b, H * (y1 - .3)], [a, H * y1]] : [[b, H * y0], [a, H * (y0 - .3)], [a, H * (y1 - .3)], [b, H * y1]], c);\n        sw(.5, .74, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .7)); sw(.5, .52, '#ffffff'); sw(.76, .8, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[1], .8));   // a swoosh in the game's colours\n        g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n        if (label && b - a >= 44) { const n = label.length, k = Math.min(4, Math.floor((H - 20) / n / 9)), y0 = Math.round(H / 2 - n * k * 4.5); for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) E.font.title(g, label[i], (a + b) / 2, y0 + i * k * 9, { align: 'center', scale: k, colors: ['#ffffff', E.shade(hue[0], .3), hue[0]], depth: 2 }); }   // the game's name down the side\n        for (let y = -24; y < H; y += 24) { const yy = Math.round(y + (t * 20) % 24); px.rect(g, right ? a + 6 : b - 10, yy, 4, 12, hue[1]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 14 : b - 18, yy + 12, 2, 6, hue[2]); }\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) { const y = (i * 61 + t * (12 + i * 3)) % (H + 20) - 10, x = right ? a + 10 + (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14) : b - 10 - (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14); px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x, y, 1 + i % 3, hue[i % 3])); }\n        px.rect(g, right ? a : b - 3, 0, 3, H, hue[0]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 3 : b - 4, 0, 1, H, '#ffffff');\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  /* =================================== 1. MAZE =================================== */\n  const MAZE = (() => {\n    const C8 = 8, MW = 29, MH = 31, TUN = 17, HX = 10, HY = 11, DOOR = [14, 10], WCOL = ['#ff4a4a', '#ff9ad8', '#4ae8ff', '#ffb84a'];\n    const CORNER = [[MW - 2, -3], [1, -3], [MW - 1, MH], [0, MH]], PHASES = [7, 20, 7, 20, 5, 20, 5, 1e9], WAYS = [[0, -1], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0]];   // (up, left, down, right: the original's order for ties)\n    let cells, grid, wgrid, start, seeds, power, hero = null, wisps = null, mode, modeT, phase, fright, eaten, level, cab, demo, over, deathT, readyT, inter, berry, ate, X0 = 0, Y0 = 12;\n    const key = (x, y) => x + ',' + y, cellOf = k => k.split(',').map(Number);\n    const nearest = (x, y, ok) => { let best = [x, y], bd = 1e9; for (let b = 0; b < MH; b++) for (let a = 0; a < MW; a++) if (ok(a, b)) { const d = Math.abs(a - x) + Math.abs(b - y); if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = [a, b]; } } return best; };\n    const ring = (x, y) => y >= HY - 1 && y <= HY + 5 && x >= HX - 1 && x <= HX + 9;\n    // a new maze: the left half from E.gen's braided maze, mirrored; doors in the middle wall; the wisps' house in a ring\n    // of hall; the tunnel's ends opened. The same level gives the same maze\n    function build() {\n      const half = E.gen.maze(15, MH, { seed: 7 + level * 13, braid: 1 }).rows;\n      cells = half.map(r => (r + r.slice(0, 14).split('').reverse().join('')).split(''));\n      for (let y = 1; y < MH - 1; y += 4) if (cells[y][13] === '.') cells[y][14] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY - 1; y <= HY + 5; y++) for (let x = HX - 1; x <= HX + 9; x++) cells[y][x] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY; y <= HY + 4; y++) for (let x = HX; x <= HX + 8; x++) cells[y][x] = y === HY || y === HY + 4 || x === HX || x === HX + 8 ? '#' : 'H';\n      cells[HY][14] = '-'; cells[TUN][0] = cells[TUN][MW - 1] = '.';\n      grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' });       // yours\n      wgrid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] !== '#' });      // the wisps' (the house too: openFor says when)\n      start = nearest(14, 23, (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y));\n      seeds = new Set(); power = new Set(); ate = 0; berry = null;\n      for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 1; x < MW - 1; x++) if (cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y) && !(x === start[0] && y === start[1])) seeds.add(key(x, y));\n      for (const [x, y] of [[1, 3], [MW - 2, 3], [1, MH - 4], [MW - 2, MH - 4]]) { const k = key(...nearest(x, y, (a, b) => seeds.has(key(a, b)))); seeds.delete(k); power.add(k); }\n    }\n    // everyone to their places: you below the house, the first wisp at its door, the others inside waiting their turn\n    function reset() {\n      hero = { m: new E.GridMover({ cx: start[0], cy: start[1], speed: 7.5 }), dir: [-1, 0], chomp: 0, dying: 0 };\n      hero.m.dir = [-1, 0];\n      const was = wisps;\n      wisps = WCOL.map((c, i) => ({ i, c, m: new E.GridMover({ cx: i ? 10 + i * 2 : DOOR[0], cy: i ? HY + 2 : DOOR[1], speed: 6.8 }), home: i > 0, wait: i * 2.5, eyes: false, leaving: false, blue: false,\n        rig: was ? was[i].rig : new E.Blob({ R: 3.6, face: 'front', colors: { dk: E.shade(c, -.35), base: c, lt: E.shade(c, .35) } }) }));\n      for (const w of wisps) w.m.dir = [w.i % 2 ? 1 : -1, 0];\n      mode = 'scatter'; modeT = 0; phase = 0; fright = 0; eaten = 0; readyT = 1.8; deathT = 0;\n    }\n    // where each aims while chasing: at you; four cells ahead of you; past a point two ahead, as far again as the first wisp\n    // is behind it (they pincer); at you from afar, its corner up close. Scattering: its corner. Eyes and leavers: the door\n    function target(w) {\n      if (w.eyes || w.leaving) return DOOR;\n      if (mode === 'scatter') return CORNER[w.i];\n      const h = hero.m, [dx, dy] = hero.dir;\n      if (w.i === 0) return [h.cx, h.cy];\n      if (w.i === 1) return [h.cx + dx * 4, h.cy + dy * 4];\n      if (w.i === 2) { const a = wisps[0].m; return [(h.cx + dx * 2) * 2 - a.cx, (h.cy + dy * 2) * 2 - a.cy]; }\n      return Math.hypot(w.m.cx - h.cx, w.m.cy - h.cy) > 8 ? [h.cx, h.cy] : CORNER[3];\n    }\n    const openFor = (w, x, y) => { if (x < 0 || x >= MW) return y === TUN; const c = cells[y] && cells[y][x]; return c === '.' || ((c === 'H' || c === '-') && (w.eyes || w.leaving)); };\n    // at each cell a wisp takes the open way (never straight back) nearest its target; blue, a random one; eyes, the\n    // grid's path home\n    function choose(w) {\n      const m = w.m;\n      if (w.eyes) { const p = grid.path([m.cx, m.cy], DOOR); if (p.length > 1) return [p[1][0] - m.cx, p[1][1] - m.cy]; }\n      const ways = WAYS.filter(([a, b]) => !(a === -m.dir[0] && b === -m.dir[1]) && openFor(w, m.cx + a, m.cy + b));\n      if (!ways.length) return [-m.dir[0], -m.dir[1]];\n      if (w.blue) return ways[Math.floor(Math.random() * ways.length)];\n      const t = target(w), d = c => (m.cx + c[0] - t[0]) ** 2 + (m.cy + c[1] - t[1]) ** 2;\n      return ways.reduce((p, q) => d(q) < d(p) ? q : p);\n    }\n    // the tunnel: off one end, on at the other, going the same way\n    function wrapTunnel(m) { if (m.cy !== TUN || m.moving) return; if (m.cx === 0 && m.dir[0] < 0) { m.place(MW - 1, TUN); m.dir = [-1, 0]; } else if (m.cx === MW - 1 && m.dir[0] > 0) { m.place(0, TUN); m.dir = [1, 0]; } }\n    const dirOf = v => Math.hypot(v[0], v[1]) < .4 ? null : Math.abs(v[0]) > Math.abs(v[1]) ? [Math.sign(v[0]), 0] : [0, Math.sign(v[1])];\n    const pos = m => ({ x: X0 + (m.x + .5) * C8, y: Y0 + (m.y + .5) * C8 });\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      if (inter) return;   // (the intermission is a script: it moves its own actors)\n      if (readyT > 0) { readyT -= dt; return; }\n      const h = hero.m;\n      if (deathT > 0) { hero.dying = deathT; if ((deathT -= dt) <= 0) lost(); return; }\n      if (fright > 0) { if ((fright -= dt) <= 0) for (const w of wisps) w.blue = false; }\n      else if ((modeT += dt) > PHASES[phase]) { modeT = 0; phase = Math.min(PHASES.length - 1, phase + 1); mode = phase % 2 ? 'chase' : 'scatter'; }\n      // you: the stick's way, kept until it can be taken (a turn asked early), going on until a wall\n      h.update(dt, grid, demo ? botDir() : dirOf(I.move()), { keep: true });\n      if (h.moving) hero.dir = h.dir;\n      wrapTunnel(h); hero.chomp = Math.max(0, hero.chomp - dt);\n      const k = key(h.cx, h.cy);\n      if (seeds.delete(k)) { cab.add(10); ate++; hero.chomp = .25; A.sfx('blip', { vol: .25, pitch: ate % 2 ? 1 : 1.2 }); if (ate === 70 || ate === 170) berry = { t: 9 }; }\n      if (power.delete(k)) { cab.add(50); fright = Math.max(1.5, 7 - level); eaten = 0; for (const w of wisps) w.blue = !w.eyes; A.sfx('powerup'); P.ring(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 2, 30, '#ffd060', .4); }\n      if (berry && (berry.t -= dt) <= 0) berry = null;\n      if (berry && h.cx === 14 && h.cy === TUN) { cab.add(100 * level, pos(h)); berry = null; A.sfx('pickup'); P.glints(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 4, 6, '#ff8a8a'); }\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const m = w.m;\n        if (w.home) { if ((w.wait -= dt) > 0) { m.y = HY + 2 + Math.sin(game.time * 6 + w.i) * .3; continue; } w.home = false; w.leaving = true; m.y = m.cy; }\n        m.speed = w.eyes ? 15 : w.blue ? 4.2 : m.cy === TUN && (m.cx < 5 || m.cx > MW - 6) ? 4 : 6.6 + level * .25;\n        m.update(dt, wgrid, m.moving ? null : choose(w), { blocked: (x, y) => !openFor(w, x, y) });\n        wrapTunnel(m);\n        if (!m.moving && m.cx === DOOR[0] && m.cy === DOOR[1]) { w.leaving = false; if (w.eyes) { w.eyes = false; w.blue = false; } }\n        if (!w.eyes && Math.abs(m.x - h.x) + Math.abs(m.y - h.y) < .8) {\n          if (w.blue) { w.eyes = true; w.blue = false; eaten++; cab.add(200 * 2 ** (eaten - 1), pos(m)); A.sfx('kick'); game.freeze(.3); P.sparks(pos(m).x, pos(m).y, 2, 8); }\n          else { deathT = 1.5; A.sfx('die'); return; }\n        }\n      }\n      if (!seeds.size && !power.size) { level++; cab.card('MAZE ' + level, 2); A.sfx('oneup'); if (level === 2 && !demo) intermission(); build(); reset(); readyT = 2.2; }\n    }\n    // after the death's turn: a life gone; the other player's maze (two players, each keeps theirs), or the end\n    function lost() {\n      const was = cab.p, r = cab.die();\n      if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; }\n      if (r === 'next') { was.save = { level, seeds, power, ate }; const s = cab.p.save; level = s ? s.level : 1; build(); if (s) ({ seeds, power, ate } = s); }\n      reset();\n    }\n    // the intermission (a script): a wisp chases you across, then you come back big and chase it\n    function intermission() {\n      const a = { x: -30, big: false }; inter = a;\n      game.script(function* () { yield game.tween(a, { x: MW * C8 + 40 }, 2.6, { ease: 'linear' }); a.big = true; yield .4; yield game.tween(a, { x: -60 }, 2.2, { ease: 'linear' }); yield .3; inter = null; });\n    }\n    // the demo's player (the attract mode, and tools/kits-test.mjs): it counts the steps to every cell, its own and the\n    // wisps' (breadth first, through the tunnel); a cell is safe when it gets there two steps before any of them. It goes\n    // the safe way to the nearest seed (a lantern when they close in, a blue wisp while there is time), else to the\n    // neighbour they reach last\n    function steps(from, ok) {\n      const D = new Map(), up = new Map(); let q = [];\n      for (const [c, d] of from) { const k = key(...c); if (!D.has(k) || D.get(k) > d) { D.set(k, d); q.push(c); } }\n      while (q.length) {\n        const n = [];\n        for (const c of q) { const d = D.get(key(...c)); for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = c[0] + a; const y = c[1] + b; if (y === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; const k = key(x, y); if (!grid.walk([x, y]) || D.has(k) || (ok && !ok(x, y, d + 1))) continue; D.set(k, d + 1); up.set(k, c); n.push([x, y]); } }\n        q = n;\n      }\n      return { D, up };\n    }\n    function botDir() {\n      const h = hero.m; if (h.moving) return null;\n      const src = [];\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        if (w.eyes || w.blue) continue;\n        if (w.home || w.leaving) { if (!w.home || w.wait < 2) src.push([DOOR, w.home ? 3 : 1]); continue; }\n        src.push([[w.m.cx, w.m.cy], 0]); const n = [w.m.cx + w.m.dir[0], w.m.cy + w.m.dir[1]]; if (grid.walk(n)) src.push([n, 0]);\n      }\n      const W = steps(src).D, wd = (x, y) => W.has(key(x, y)) ? W.get(key(x, y)) : 99, safe = (x, y, d) => d + 2 < wd(x, y);\n      const S = steps([[[h.cx, h.cy], 0]], safe), near = wd(h.cx, h.cy) < 7;\n      const goals = fright > 2.5 && wisps.some(w => w.blue) ? wisps.filter(w => w.blue).map(w => key(w.m.cx, w.m.cy)) : near && [...power].some(k => S.D.has(k)) ? [...power] : [...seeds, ...power];\n      let best = null, bd = 1e9; for (const k of goals) { const d = S.D.get(k); if (d > 0 && d < bd) { bd = d; best = k; } }\n      if (best) { let c = cellOf(best), p; while ((p = S.up.get(key(...c))) && !(p[0] === h.cx && p[1] === h.cy)) c = p; return [Math.sign(E.wrapDiff(h.cx, c[0], MW)), c[1] - h.cy]; }\n      let far = null, fd = -1;\n      for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = h.cx + a; if (h.cy === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; if (grid.walk([x, h.cy + b]) && wd(x, h.cy + b) > fd) { fd = wd(x, h.cy + b); far = [a, b]; } }\n      return far;\n    }\n    function layout() { X0 = Math.round((game.W - MW * C8) / 2); Y0 = Math.max(12, Math.round((game.H - MH * C8) / 2)); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), t = game.time, [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), bx = ox + X0, by = oy + Y0;\n      r.sky(cl ? ['#000000', '#000000'] : ['#04030c', '#0a0820', '#120a28']);\n      // the maze on the floor (lit in the remaster: hedges with a sunlit top edge and a shadow at the foot; the classic's\n      // thin blue lines facing the halls)\n      r.decal(g => {\n        const wall = (x, y) => !!cells[y] && cells[y][x] === '#';\n        for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n          const c = cells[y][x], X = bx + x * C8, Y = by + y * C8;\n          if (c === '#') {\n            if (cl) { px.col(g, '#2121de'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + 2, C8, 1); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + C8 - 3, C8, 1); if (!wall(x - 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + 2, Y, 1, C8); if (!wall(x + 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + C8 - 3, Y, 1, C8); }\n            else { px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, '#1c4a22'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, 2, '#5aa84a'); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y + C8 - 2, C8, 2, '#0c2410'); if (E.hash2(x, y) < .3) px.dot(g, X + 2 + (x * 3) % 4, Y + 3 + (y * 5) % 3, '#7ac860'); }\n          } else if (c === '-') px.rect(g, X, Y + 3, C8, 2, cl ? '#ffb8ff' : '#e0a0ff');\n          else if (!cl) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, (x + y) % 2 ? '#141026' : '#171230');\n        }\n      });\n      // the seeds, lanterns and the berry: glowing (they stay bright under the light)\n      r.queue(0, -1e4, 0, g => {\n        for (const k of seeds) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 3, Y = by + y * C8 + 3; px.rect(g, X, Y, 2, 2, cl ? '#ffb897' : '#ffe9a0'); if (!cl) px.dot(g, X, Y, '#ffffff'); }\n        if (Math.floor(t * 4) % 2 || readyT > 0) for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 4, Y = by + y * C8 + 4; if (cl) px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#ffb897'); else { px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, X, Y, 6, '#ffb030')); px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#fff4c0'); } }\n        if (berry) { const X = bx + 14 * C8 + 4, Y = by + TUN * C8 + 4; px.disc(g, X - 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.disc(g, X + 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.dot(g, X - 2, Y, '#ffb0b0'); px.rect(g, X - 1, Y - 3, 3, 1, '#4ad84a'); }\n      }, { emissive: true, bias: -1e6 });\n      if (!cl) { L.add(pos(hero.m).x, pos(hero.m).y, 8, 60, 1.2, { color: '#ffe890' }); for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k); L.add(X0 + x * C8 + 4, Y0 + y * C8 + 4, 6, 26, .7, { color: '#ffb040' }); } }\n      if (inter) { drawInter(r); return; }\n      // you: a lit sphere with a chomping mouth (classic: the flat yellow disc); dying, the mouth opens until you are gone\n      const hp = pos(hero.m), ang = Math.atan2(hero.dir[1], hero.dir[0]), open = hero.dying > 0 ? Math.PI * (1 - hero.dying / 1.5) : (hero.m.moving || hero.chomp > 0 ? Math.abs(Math.sin(t * 16)) : .3) * .9;\n      if (hero.dying <= 0 || open < Math.PI * .98) r.actor(hp.x, hp.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n        y -= 0; const R = 4;\n        if (cl) px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#ffe000'); else { px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#d8a010'); px.disc(g, x - .5, y - .5, R - 1, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 1.5, y - 1.5, 1.5, '#fff8c0'); }\n        if (open > .05) px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x + Math.cos(ang - open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang - open) * 7], [x + Math.cos(ang) * 8, y + Math.sin(ang) * 8], [x + Math.cos(ang + open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang + open) * 7]], cl ? '#000000' : '#141026');\n      }, { outline: !cl, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n      if (deathT > 0) return;\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const p = pos(w.m), blink = w.blue && fright < 2 && Math.floor(t * 6) % 2, body = w.blue ? (blink ? '#f0f0ff' : '#2a3aff') : w.c;\n        if (w.eyes || cl) r.actor(p.x, p.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n          if (!w.eyes) { px.disc(g, x, y - 1, 4, body); px.rect(g, x - 4, y - 1, 9, 4, body); for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.dot(g, x - 3 + i * 3 + (Math.floor(t * 8) % 2), y + 3, '#000000'); }\n          if (w.blue && !w.eyes) { px.rect(g, x - 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); px.rect(g, x + 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); return; }\n          const [dx, dy] = w.m.dir; px.rect(g, x - 3, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, x - 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff'); px.dot(g, x + 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff');\n        }, { outline: false, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n        else {   // a Blob rig, its colour its own (blue while you can eat it), its eyes on the way it goes\n          const rig = w.rig; rig.C.base = body; rig.C.dk = E.shade(body, -.35); rig.C.lt = E.shade(body, .35);\n          rig.update(1 / 60, { look: w.m.dir, walk: 1, squash: Math.sin(t * 10 + w.i) * .08 });\n          r.actor(p.x, p.y + 3, 0, (g, x, y) => rig.draw(g, x, y, E.VIEWS.threequarter), { outline: true, rim: true, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n          if (w.blue) L.add(p.x, p.y, 6, 22, .5, { color: '#6a7aff' });\n        }\n      }\n      if (readyT > 0) r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, 'READY!', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + (HY + 6) * C8 + 1, '#ffe040', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' }));\n    }\n    function drawInter(r) {\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        const a = inter, y = Y0 + TUN * C8 + 4, x = X0 + a.x;\n        E.font.text(g, 'INTERMISSION', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + 8 * C8, '#ffe070', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' });\n        if (!a.big) { px.disc(g, x, y, 4, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 20, y - 1, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, x - 24, y - 1, 9, 4, '#ff4a4a'); }\n        else { px.disc(g, x + 30, y - 1, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.rect(g, x + 26, y - 1, 9, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.disc(g, x, y, 11, '#ffe040'); px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x - 12, y - 6], [x - 12, y + 6]], '#000000'); }\n      });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'maze', label: 'MAZE', res: [232, 270], about: 'EAT EVERY SEED, DODGE FOUR WISPS', hue: ['#ffe040', '#4ae8ff', '#ff4a8a'], touch: [], extra: [10000], light: .5,\n      begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; over = false; level = 1; inter = null; wisps = wisps || null; build(); reset(); },\n      revive() { over = false; reset(); },   // after a continue: the same maze, everyone back in place\n      force() { over = true; },\n      step, draw, box: () => [X0, Y0 - 12, MW * C8, MH * C8 + 22], edges: () => [X0 - 4, X0 + MW * C8 + 4],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return level; },\n      state: () => ({ hero: [hero.m.cx, hero.m.cy], wisps: wisps.map(w => [w.m.cx, w.m.cy, w.eyes, w.blue]), seeds: seeds.size + power.size, level, fright: +fright.toFixed(3) })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 2. FORMATION =================================== */\n  const FORM = (() => {\n    const FW = 224, FLY = 130;   // the field's width (its height is the screen's: FH), a moth's speed along its path (px/s)\n    let FH = 270;\n    const MOTH = {\n      a: E.sprite(['..y..y..', '.yYyyYy.', 'ybbBBbby', 'bbBwwBbb', '.bBBBBb.', '..b..b..'], { y: '#ffe040', Y: '#fff8a0', b: '#4a8aff', B: '#8ab8ff', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      b: E.sprite(['r......r', '.rRRRRr.', 'rRwRRwRr', '.rRRRRr.', 'r.r..r.r'], { r: '#e03a4a', R: '#ff8a8a', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      boss: E.sprite(['..gGGg..', '.gGwwGg.', 'gGGGGGGg', 'gpGppGpg', '.p.pp.p.', 'p......p'], { g: '#3ad860', G: '#9af0a0', w: '#ffffff', p: '#c050f0' }),\n      hurt: E.sprite(['..pPPp..', '.pPwwPp.', 'pPPPPPPp', 'pgPggPgp', '.g.gg.g.', 'g......g'], { p: '#a050e0', P: '#d8a0ff', w: '#ffffff', g: '#3ad860' })\n    };\n    const SHIP = E.sprite(['...w...', '...w...', '..wrw..', '.wwrww.', 'wwbwbww', 'w.bbb.w', 'r..r..r'], { w: '#f0f0f8', r: '#ff4a4a', b: '#4a8aff' });\n    const ROWS = [['boss', 4], ['b', 8], ['b', 8], ['a', 10], ['a', 10]];\n    const SLOTS = ROWS.flatMap(([kind, n], row) => Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => ({ kind, x: FW / 2 + (i - (n - 1) / 2) * 18, y: 36 + row * 16 })));\n    let cab, demo, foes, shots, bombs, ship, wave, sway, dead, over, readyT, stars = [], X0 = 0, Y0 = 0;\n    // a wave: five groups of eight fly in from alternate sides, a loop on the way, each to its own place (Catmull paths)\n    function newWave() {\n      foes = []; wave++; cab.card('STAGE ' + wave, 1.8); readyT = Math.max(readyT, .6);\n      SLOTS.forEach((s, i) => {\n        const group = Math.floor(i / 8), side = group % 2 ? 1 : -1, k = i % 8;\n        const path = new E.Path([[FW / 2 + side * 150, -20], [FW / 2 + side * 70, 80], [FW / 2 - side * 20, 170], [FW / 2 - side * 70, 120], [FW / 2 - side * 30, 70], [s.x, s.y]], { smooth: 'catmull' });\n        foes.push({ kind: s.kind, hp: s.kind === 'boss' ? 2 : 1, slot: s, path, d: -(group * 1.6 + k * .14) * FLY, state: 'in', x: path.at(0).x, y: -20, a: Math.PI / 2 });\n      });\n    }\n    function begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; wave = 0; over = false; shots = []; bombs = []; sway = 0; dead = 0; readyT = 1.4; ship = { x: FW / 2, y: FH - 28, cool: 0 }; stars = Array.from({ length: 90 }, (_, i) => ({ x: (i * 97) % FW, y: (i * 53) % 600, s: 20 + (i % 3) * 25 })); layout(); newWave(); }\n    // a dive: from its place a swoop out, at the ship (where it is now) and off the bottom; it comes back from the top\n    function dive(f) {\n      const sx = ship.x, out = f.x < FW / 2 ? -1 : 1;\n      f.path = new E.Path([[f.x, f.y], [f.x + out * 30, f.y - 16], [f.x + out * 46, f.y + 20], [sx + (Math.random() - .5) * 50, FH * .62], [sx + out * 40, FH + 24]], { smooth: 'catmull' }); f.d = 0; f.state = 'dive';\n    }\n    const kill = f => { f.hp = 0; cab.add(f.kind === 'boss' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 400 : 150) : f.kind === 'b' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 160 : 80) : (f.state === 'dive' ? 100 : 50), { x: X0 + f.x, y: Y0 + f.y }); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 10); P.bits(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 6, ['#ffe040', '#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a']); A.sfx('explode', { vol: .45 }); };\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      layout(); sway += dt; ship.y = FH - 28;\n      for (const s of stars) s.y = (s.y + s.s * dt) % 600;\n      if (readyT > 0) readyT -= dt;\n      if (dead > 0 && (dead -= dt) <= 0) { const was = cab.p, r = cab.die(); if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; } if (r === 'next') { was.save = { wave, foes }; const s = cab.p.save; if (s) { wave = s.wave; foes = s.foes; for (const f of foes) if (f.state !== 'form') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; } } else { wave = 0; newWave(); } } ship.x = FW / 2; bombs.length = 0; readyT = 1.4; }\n      const live = dead <= 0 && readyT <= 0;\n      if (live) {   // the ship: left and right; two shots on screen at most\n        const mv = demo ? botMove() : I.move()[0]; ship.x = clamp(ship.x + mv * 115 * dt, 10, FW - 10); ship.cool -= dt;\n        if ((demo ? botFire() : I.down('fire')) && ship.cool <= 0 && shots.length < 2) { shots.push({ x: ship.x, y: ship.y - 8 }); ship.cool = .2; A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .35 }); }\n      }\n      for (const s of shots) s.y -= 270 * dt; shots = shots.filter(s => s.y > -10);\n      const sx = Math.sin(sway * 1.2) * 12;\n      let formed = 0;\n      for (const f of foes) {\n        if (f.state === 'in' || f.state === 'dive') {\n          f.d += FLY * (1 + wave * .04) * dt; if (f.d < 0) continue;\n          const p = f.path.at(f.d), u = f.state === 'in' ? Math.min(1, f.d / f.path.length) : 0; f.x = p.x + sx * u * u; f.y = p.y; f.a = p.angle;\n          if (f.d >= f.path.length) { if (f.state === 'dive') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; f.x = f.slot.x + sx; } else f.state = 'form'; }\n          if (f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50 && Math.random() < dt * (.7 + wave * .1)) bombs.push({ x: f.x, y: f.y, vx: (ship.x - f.x) * .35, vy: 125 });\n        } else if (f.state === 'back') { f.y += 90 * dt; f.x += (f.slot.x + sx - f.x) * Math.min(1, dt * 4); f.a = Math.PI / 2; if (f.y >= f.slot.y) f.state = 'form'; }\n        else { f.x = f.slot.x + sx; f.y = f.slot.y + Math.sin(sway * 3 + f.slot.x * .1) * 1.5; f.a = Math.PI / 2; formed++; }\n      }\n      if (live && formed > 3 && Math.random() < dt * (.45 + wave * .15)) { const c = foes.filter(f => f.state === 'form' && f.hp > 0); if (c.length) { const f = c[Math.floor(Math.random() * c.length)]; dive(f); if (f.kind === 'boss') for (const e of c.filter(e => e !== f && e.kind === 'b' && Math.abs(e.slot.x - f.slot.x) < 20).slice(0, 2)) dive(e); A.sfx('whoosh', { vol: .3 }); } }\n      for (const b of bombs) { b.x += b.vx * dt; b.y += b.vy * dt; } bombs = bombs.filter(b => b.y < FH + 10);\n      for (const s of shots) for (const f of foes) if (!s.hit && f.hp > 0 && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(s.x - f.x) < 7 && Math.abs(s.y - f.y) < 6) { s.hit = true; if (--f.hp > 0) { A.sfx('bump'); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 4); } else kill(f); }\n      shots = shots.filter(s => !s.hit); foes = foes.filter(f => f.hp > 0);\n      if (live) for (const o of [...bombs, ...foes]) if (Math.abs(o.x - ship.x) < 6 && Math.abs(o.y - ship.y) < 6) { dead = 1.8; P.explosion(X0 + ship.x, Y0 + ship.y, 4, .9, { sound: true, flash: false, shake: 2, freeze: false }); if (o.hp) kill(o); break; }\n      if (!foes.length && dead <= 0) newWave();\n    }\n    // the demo's pilot: of a step left, none and a step right, the first where no bomb or diving moth will be in the next\n    // half second (a bomb's way read ahead to the ship's row), preferring the way to the moth nearest above; firing when\n    // under one\n    const hitAt = (x, t) => bombs.some(b => { const k = (ship.y - b.y) / b.vy; return k > -.05 && k < t && Math.abs(b.x + b.vx * k - x) < 9; }) || foes.some(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.y - ship.y) < 40 && Math.abs(f.x - x) < 12);\n    const botMove = () => {\n      const t = foes.find(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50) || foes.filter(f => f.d >= 0).reduce((p, f) => !p || Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < Math.abs(p.x - ship.x) ? f : p, null);\n      const want = t ? clamp((t.x - ship.x) / 10, -1, 1) : 0, ways = [want, 0, -1, 1].map(m => Math.round(m)), q = m => clamp(ship.x + m * 115 * .3, 10, FW - 10);\n      for (const m of ways) if (!hitAt(q(m), .8) && !hitAt((ship.x + q(m)) / 2, .4)) return m === Math.round(want) ? want : m;\n      return ship.x < FW / 2 ? 1 : -1;\n    };\n    const botFire = () => foes.some(f => f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < 8);\n    function layout() { FH = Math.max(270, game.H - 4); X0 = Math.round((game.W - FW) / 2); Y0 = Math.round((game.H - FH) / 2); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), x0 = X0, y0 = Y0;\n      if (cl) r.sky(['#000000', '#000000']); else {\n        SPACE[0].draw(r);\n        r.decal(g => {   // a ringed gas giant low in the field, lit from the upper right: the ring's far half, the planet's banded\n          // shading (discs stepped toward the light), the ring's near half\n          const [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), cx = Math.round(ox + x0 + FW * .24), cy = Math.round(oy + y0 + FH - 40), R = 40;\n          const ring = near => { for (let a = 0; a < TAU; a += .012) { if ((Math.sin(a) > 0) !== near) continue; for (const [k, c] of [[1.55, '#8a6aa8'], [1.7, '#c8a8e0'], [1.85, '#6a4a88']]) px.dot(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * R * k, cy + Math.sin(a) * R * k * .22, c); } };\n          ring(false);\n          ['#1a1030', '#2a1a46', '#3e2860', '#563a7a', '#704e94', '#8c66ac', '#a882c2'].forEach((c, k) => px.disc(g, cx + k * 1.4, cy - k * 1.4, R - k * 4.5, c));\n          for (let b = -2; b <= 2; b++) { const y = b * 12 + 3, hw = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, (R - 2) ** 2 - y * y)) - 3; px.blend(g, .16, 'normal', () => px.rect(g, cx - hw + 1, cy + y, hw * 2, 2, b % 2 ? '#2a1640' : '#e8c8a0')); }\n          ring(true);\n        });\n      }\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        for (const s of stars) if (s.y < FH) px.dot(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, s.s > 50 ? '#ffffff' : s.s > 30 ? '#8a8ab0' : '#4a4a6a');\n        for (const s of shots) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .5, 'add', () => px.rect(g, x0 + s.x - 1, y0 + s.y - 1, 3, 7, '#8ad8ff')); px.rect(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 1, 5, '#ffffff'); }\n        for (const b of bombs) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .4, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x0 + b.x, y0 + b.y, 3, '#ff8a4a')); px.rect(g, x0 + b.x - 1, y0 + b.y - 1, 2, 4, '#ff6a4a'); }\n      });\n      // each moth turned to the way it flies (r.sprite's rot; in its place, facing down); the classic turns in 16 steps\n      for (const f of foes) if (f.d >= 0 || f.state !== 'in') r.sprite(x0 + f.x, y0 + f.y, 0, f.kind === 'boss' && f.hp === 1 ? MOTH.hurt : MOTH[f.kind], { rot: f.a + Math.PI / 2, anchor: 'center', steps: cl ? 16 : 32, glow: cl ? 0 : .3 });\n      if (dead <= 0 && !over && (readyT <= 0 || Math.floor(readyT * 8) % 2)) r.sprite(x0 + ship.x, y0 + ship.y, 0, SHIP, { anchor: 'center', glow: cl ? 0 : .4 });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'formation', label: 'FORMATION', res: [232, 270], about: 'MOTHS FLY IN, FORM UP AND DIVE', hue: ['#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a', '#ffe040'], touch: ['fire'], extra: [20000, 70000], light: 0, fills: true,\n      begin, revive() { over = false; ship.x = FW / 2; bombs.length = 0; readyT = 1.4; }, force() { over = true; }, step, draw,\n      box: () => [X0, Y0, FW, FH], edges: () => [X0 - 2, X0 + FW + 2],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return wave; },\n      state: () => ({ ship: +ship.x.toFixed(2), foes: foes.length, wave, shots: shots.length, bombs: bombs.length })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 3. ROCKS =================================== */\n  const ROCKS = (() => {\n    let RW = 320, RH = 240;   // the field: the whole screen (at least 320 x 240), its edges meeting\n    let cab, demo, ship, rocks, shots, saucer, over, wave, deadT, readyT, sparks, X0 = 0, Y0 = 0;\n    // a rock: a ring of lumpy points; size 3 big, 2, 1 small; the smaller, the faster\n    const rock = (x, y, size) => { const n = 8 + size * 2, R = [0, 5, 10, 18][size], a = Math.random() * TAU, sp = (52 - size * 11) * (.6 + Math.random() * .6); return { x, y, vx: Math.cos(a) * sp, vy: Math.sin(a) * sp, size, R, rot: 0, spin: (Math.random() - .5) * 2, pts: Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => { const t = i / n * TAU, k = .75 + Math.random() * .35; return [Math.cos(t) * R * k, Math.sin(t) * R * k]; }) }; };\n    function newWave() { wave++; rocks = []; for (let i = 0; i < 3 + wave; i++) { const edge = Math.random() < .5; rocks.push(rock(edge ? 0 : Math.random() * RW, edge ? Math.random() * RH : 0, 3)); } if (wave > 1) cab.card('WAVE ' + wave, 1.4); }\n    const home = () => Object.assign(ship, { x: RW / 2, y: RH / 2, vx: 0, vy: 0, a: -Math.PI / 2 });\n    function begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; wave = 0; over = false; shots = []; saucer = null; sparks = []; deadT = 0; readyT = 1.2; ship = { cool: 0, thrust: false }; layout(); home(); newWave(); }\n    const wd = (a, b, s) => E.wrapDiff(a, b, s), far = (a, b) => Math.hypot(wd(a.x, b.x, RW), wd(a.y, b.y, RH));\n    const burst = (x, y, n, sp, life, c) => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const a = Math.random() * TAU, v = sp * (.4 + Math.random() * .6); sparks.push({ x, y, vx: Math.cos(a) * v, vy: Math.sin(a) * v, t: life * (.5 + Math.random() * .5), c }); } };\n    function kill() { deadT = 1.8; A.sfx('boom'); burst(ship.x, ship.y, 24, 80, .9, '#ffe0a0'); game.shake(3); }\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      layout(); if (readyT > 0 && (readyT > .3 || !rocks.some(k => far(k, { x: RW / 2, y: RH / 2 }) < k.R + 40))) readyT -= dt;   // (it comes back once the middle is clear)\n      if (deadT > 0 && (deadT -= dt) <= 0) { const was = cab.p, r = cab.die(); if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; } if (r === 'next') { was.save = { wave, rocks }; const s = cab.p.save; if (s) ({ wave, rocks } = s); else { wave = 0; newWave(); } } home(); readyT = 1.4; shots = shots.filter(s => !s.foe); }\n      const live = deadT <= 0 && readyT <= 0;\n      if (live) {   // turn, thrust (and drift: a little drag), fire, hyperspace (a one-in-ten chance it goes wrong)\n        const turn = demo ? botTurn() : I.move()[0], thr = demo ? botThrust() : I.down('up') || I.down('thrust') || I.move()[1] < -.6;\n        ship.a += turn * 4.4 * dt; ship.thrust = thr;\n        if (thr) { ship.vx += Math.cos(ship.a) * 170 * dt; ship.vy += Math.sin(ship.a) * 170 * dt; if (Math.random() < .6) sparks.push({ x: ship.x - Math.cos(ship.a) * 6, y: ship.y - Math.sin(ship.a) * 6, vx: -Math.cos(ship.a) * 50 + (Math.random() - .5) * 24, vy: -Math.sin(ship.a) * 50 + (Math.random() - .5) * 24, t: .3, c: '#ffb84a' }); }\n        const sp = Math.hypot(ship.vx, ship.vy); if (sp > 220) { ship.vx *= 220 / sp; ship.vy *= 220 / sp; }\n        ship.vx *= Math.exp(-.4 * dt); ship.vy *= Math.exp(-.4 * dt); ship.cool -= dt;\n        if ((demo ? botFire() : I.pressed('fire')) && ship.cool <= 0 && shots.filter(s => !s.foe).length < 5) { shots.push({ x: ship.x + Math.cos(ship.a) * 7, y: ship.y + Math.sin(ship.a) * 7, vx: Math.cos(ship.a) * 290 + ship.vx, vy: Math.sin(ship.a) * 290 + ship.vy, t: .85 }); ship.cool = .12; A.sfx('laser', { vol: .3 }); }\n        if (demo ? botWarp() : I.pressed('warp')) { burst(ship.x, ship.y, 10, 40, .4, '#8ab8ff'); ship.x = Math.random() * RW; ship.y = Math.random() * RH; ship.vx = ship.vy = 0; A.sfx('warp'); if (Math.random() < .1) kill(); }\n      }\n      if (deadT <= 0) { ship.x = E.wrap(ship.x + ship.vx * dt, 0, RW); ship.y = E.wrap(ship.y + ship.vy * dt, 0, RH); }\n      for (const s of shots) { s.x = E.wrap(s.x + s.vx * dt, 0, RW); s.y = E.wrap(s.y + s.vy * dt, 0, RH); s.t -= dt; }\n      for (const k of rocks) { k.x = E.wrap(k.x + k.vx * dt, 0, RW); k.y = E.wrap(k.y + k.vy * dt, 0, RH); k.rot += k.spin * dt; }\n      for (const p of sparks) { p.x += p.vx * dt; p.y += p.vy * dt; p.t -= dt; } sparks = sparks.filter(p => p.t > 0);\n      // the saucer: now and then, across the screen, shooting at you (across the edges: the nearer way)\n      if (!saucer && live && Math.random() < dt * .05 * wave) saucer = { x: 0, y: 30 + Math.random() * (RH - 60), vx: Math.random() < .5 ? 60 : -60, vy: 0, t: 0, cool: 1.2 };\n      if (saucer) {\n        saucer.x = E.wrap(saucer.x + saucer.vx * dt, 0, RW); saucer.t += dt; saucer.vy = Math.sin(saucer.t * 2) * 22; saucer.y = E.wrap(saucer.y + saucer.vy * dt, 0, RH); saucer.cool -= dt;\n        if (saucer.cool <= 0 && live) { const a = Math.atan2(wd(saucer.y, ship.y, RH), wd(saucer.x, ship.x, RW)) + (Math.random() - .5) * .5; shots.push({ x: saucer.x, y: saucer.y, vx: Math.cos(a) * 150, vy: Math.sin(a) * 150, t: 1.4, foe: true }); saucer.cool = 1.4; A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .2, pitch: .6 }); }\n        if (saucer.t > RW / 60) saucer = null;\n      }\n      // hits: your shots split rocks (big 20, middle 50, small 100) and down the saucer (500); rocks, its shots and it on you\n      for (const s of shots) {\n        if (s.t <= 0 || s.foe) continue;\n        for (const k of rocks) if (!k.dead && far(s, k) < k.R) { k.dead = true; s.t = 0; cab.add([0, 100, 50, 20][k.size], { x: X0 + k.x, y: Y0 + k.y }); A.sfx(k.size > 2 ? 'boom' : 'explode', { vol: .4 }); burst(k.x, k.y, 6 + k.size * 3, 60, .6, '#c8d8ff'); if (k.size > 1) for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) rocks.push(rock(k.x, k.y, k.size - 1)); break; }\n        if (s.t > 0 && saucer && far(s, saucer) < 8) { cab.add(500, { x: X0 + saucer.x, y: Y0 + saucer.y }); s.t = 0; burst(saucer.x, saucer.y, 16, 70, .7, '#ff8aa8'); saucer = null; A.sfx('boom'); }\n      }\n      rocks = rocks.filter(k => !k.dead); shots = shots.filter(s => s.t > 0);\n      if (live && (rocks.some(k => far(ship, k) < k.R + 4) || shots.some(s => s.foe && far(s, ship) < 5) || (saucer && far(saucer, ship) < 10))) kill();\n      if (!rocks.length) newWave();\n    }\n    // the demo's pilot: a rock, the saucer or its shot that will pass within reach in the next second and a half is a\n    // threat: turn across its way and thrust out of it (hyperspace when it is a quarter second off); else brake when\n    // drifting, and turn to where the nearest rock will be when a shot gets there (across the edges), firing when facing\n    // it; the saucer first when it is about\n    function threat() {\n      let worst = null, wt = 1.5;\n      const all = [...rocks, ...(saucer ? [Object.assign({ R: 9 }, saucer)] : []), ...shots.filter(s => s.foe).map(s => Object.assign({ R: 3 }, s))];\n      for (const k of all) {\n        const rx = wd(ship.x, k.x, RW), ry = wd(ship.y, k.y, RH), vx = k.vx - ship.vx, vy = k.vy - ship.vy, v2 = vx * vx + vy * vy || 1, t = -(rx * vx + ry * vy) / v2;\n        if (Math.hypot(rx, ry) < k.R + 12) return { k, t: 0, a: Math.atan2(-ry, -rx) };\n        if (t > 0 && t < wt && Math.hypot(rx + vx * t, ry + vy * t) < k.R + 9) { wt = t; worst = { k, t, a: Math.atan2(vy, vx) + (vx * ry - vy * rx > 0 ? -1 : 1) * Math.PI / 2 }; }\n      }\n      return worst;\n    }\n    const brake = () => Math.hypot(ship.vx, ship.vy) > 45 ? Math.atan2(-ship.vy, -ship.vx) : null;\n    function aim() {\n      let b = null, bd = 1e9; for (const k of saucer ? [saucer] : rocks) { const d = far(ship, k); if (d < bd) { bd = d; b = k; } }\n      if (!b) return null; const t = bd / 290; return Math.atan2(wd(ship.y, b.y + b.vy * t, RH), wd(ship.x, b.x + b.vx * t, RW));\n    }\n    const botTurn = () => { const th = threat(), b = brake(), a = th ? th.a : b !== null ? b : aim(); return a === null ? 0 : clamp(E.angDiff(ship.a, a) * 4, -1, 1); };\n    const botFire = () => { const a = aim(); return a !== null && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, a)) < .15; };\n    const botThrust = () => { const th = threat(), b = brake(), a = th ? th.a : b; return a !== null && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, a)) < .6; };\n    const botWarp = () => { const th = threat(); return !!th && th.t < .25 && th.k.R > 3 && Math.abs(E.angDiff(ship.a, th.a)) > 1; };\n    function layout() { RW = Math.max(320, game.W); RH = Math.max(240, game.H); X0 = Math.round((game.W - RW) / 2); Y0 = Math.round((game.H - RH) / 2); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), x0 = X0, y0 = Y0;\n      if (cl) r.sky(['#000000', '#000000']); else SPACE[1].draw(r);\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(x0, y0, RW, RH); g.clip();\n        // glowing vector lines: each shape bright over a soft wide glow (classic: plain white lines), at every edge it crosses\n        const vec = (pts, x, y, a, color, closed = true) => {\n          for (const ox of [-RW, 0, RW]) for (const oy of [-RH, 0, RH]) {\n            const Q = pts.map(([u, v]) => [x0 + x + ox + u * Math.cos(a) - v * Math.sin(a), y0 + y + oy + u * Math.sin(a) + v * Math.cos(a)]);\n            if (Q.every(q => q[0] < x0 - 2 || q[0] > x0 + RW + 2) || Q.every(q => q[1] < y0 - 2 || q[1] > y0 + RH + 2)) continue;\n            const n = closed ? Q.length : Q.length - 1;\n            if (!cl) px.blend(g, .3, 'add', () => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) px.line(g, ...Q[i], ...Q[(i + 1) % Q.length], color, 3); });\n            for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) px.line(g, ...Q[i], ...Q[(i + 1) % Q.length], cl ? '#ffffff' : E.shade(color, .45));\n          }\n        };\n        for (const k of rocks) vec(k.pts, k.x, k.y, k.rot, '#8ab8ff');\n        if (deadT <= 0 && (readyT <= 0 || Math.floor(readyT * 8) % 2)) { vec([[8, 0], [-6, -5], [-3, 0], [-6, 5]], ship.x, ship.y, ship.a, '#ffffff'); if (ship.thrust && Math.floor(game.time * 30) % 2) vec([[-4, -2], [-9, 0], [-4, 2]], ship.x, ship.y, ship.a, '#ffb84a', false); }\n        if (saucer) vec([[-9, 0], [-4, -3], [4, -3], [9, 0], [4, 3], [-4, 3], [-9, 0], [9, 0], [4, -3], [2, -6], [-2, -6], [-4, -3]], saucer.x, saucer.y, 0, '#ff6a8a', false);\n        for (const s of shots) { if (!cl) px.blend(g, .5, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 2, s.foe ? '#ff6a8a' : '#c8e0ff')); px.rect(g, x0 + s.x, y0 + s.y, 1, 1, '#ffffff'); }\n        for (const p of sparks) px.dot(g, x0 + p.x, y0 + p.y, cl ? '#ffffff' : p.c);\n        g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n      });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'rocks', label: 'ROCKS', res: [320, 240], about: 'TURN, THRUST, SPLIT THE ROCKS', hue: ['#c8d8ff', '#8ab8ff', '#ff8a4a'], touch: ['fire', 'thrust', 'warp'], every: 10000, light: 0, fills: true,\n      begin, revive() { over = false; home(); readyT = 1.4; }, force() { over = true; }, step, draw,\n      box: () => [X0, Y0, RW, RH], edges: () => [X0 - 2, X0 + RW + 2],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return wave; },\n      state: () => ({ ship: [+ship.x.toFixed(2), +ship.y.toFixed(2)], rocks: rocks.length, wave, shots: shots.length })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 4. THE CABINET: a scene per game, the title, the attract mode =================================== */\n  const GAMES = [MAZE, FORM, ROCKS];\n  const cabs = {}; for (const G of GAMES) cabs[G.id] = new E.Arcade(game, { id: G.id, lives: 3, extra: G.extra || [], every: G.every });\n  const front = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'arcade', idle: 20, demo: 1e9, scores: 6 });   // the title's attract clock (a demo ends itself: endDemo)\n  let pick = 0, players = 1, demoNext = 0, cabsAt = [];\n  function playScene(G) {\n    const cab = cabs[G.id];\n    let demo = false, demoT = 0, stage = 'play', tableT = 0;\n    // the end: each player's initials in turn (the best first) where they make the table, then the table\n    const ending = (order = cab.players.slice().sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score)) => {\n      const p = order.shift(); if (!p) { stage = 'table'; tableT = 0; A.music(null); return; }\n      if (cab.qualifies(p.score)) { stage = 'entry'; if (cab.players.length > 1) cab.say('PLAYER ' + p.n, 30); cab.enter(p.score, '', () => { cab.clear(); ending(order); }); } else ending(order);\n    };\n    const scene = {\n      view: 'overhead', views: ['overhead'], input: KEYS, res: G.res, expand: true, pausable: true, touch: G.touch, camera: { zoom: false },\n      enter(d) {\n        demo = !!(d && d.demo); demoT = 0; stage = 'play'; tableT = 0;\n        game.follow(null); game.cam.bounds = null; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0); game.cam.snap = true;\n        L.enabled = !classic() && G.light > 0; L.ambient = G.light; L.dark = [4, 2, 14]; L.refresh();\n        if (G.id === 'rocks') { game.input.touchSet('thrust', 'THRUST'); game.input.touchSet('warp', 'WARP'); }\n        cab.start(demo ? 1 : players, { demo }); G.begin(cab, demo); A.music(null);\n      },\n      exit() { L.enabled = false; },\n      back() { game.go('arcade'); return true; },\n      update(dt) {\n        const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\n        if (I.pressed('classic')) { game.settings.set('arcadeLook', classic() ? 'remaster' : 'classic'); L.enabled = !classic() && G.light > 0; game.note(classic() ? 'CLASSIC LOOK' : 'REMASTER'); }\n        cab.update(dt);\n        if (demo) { demoT += dt; if (I.anyPressed() || I.clicked() || demoT > 30 || G.over) { front.endDemo(); game.go('arcade', { scores: G.id }, { fade: 'black' }); return; } G.step(dt, I); return; }\n        if (cab.entry || cab.continuing) return;\n        if (stage === 'table') { tableT += dt; if (tableT > 8 || (tableT > 1 && (I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start') || I.clicked()))) game.go('arcade', null, { fade: 'black' }); return; }\n        if (G.over && stage === 'play') { stage = 'cont'; cab.continue(9, yes => { if (yes) { stage = 'play'; G.revive(); } else ending(); }); return; }\n        G.step(dt, I);\n      },\n      draw(r) {\n        G.draw(r); const [e0, e1] = G.edges(), b = G.box(); cabinet(r, e0, e1, G.hue, G.fills ? 0 : b[1], G.fills ? r.H : b[1] + b[3], G.label);\n        if (stage === 'table') { r.overlay(g => { g.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.78)'; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); px.reset(g); }); cab.drawTable(r, '', Math.max(16, Math.round(r.H / 2 - 82)), G.label + ' HIGH SCORES'); }\n        else cab.draw(r, G.box());\n      },\n      /** the end of a game, now, with score (tools/phone-test.mjs: the way to the table): lives to none; the continue when\n       *  cont, else straight to the initials */\n      end(score, cont) { cab.p.score = score; cab.hi = Math.max(cab.hi, score); for (const p of cab.players) p.lives = 0; G.force(); if (!cont) { stage = 'cont'; ending(); } },\n      /** the proof: a scripted game, a hash of where things are and the scores */\n      run: (n = 600) => proof('arcade-' + G.id, n, (i, k) => { walk(i, k, ['left', 'up', 'right', 'down'], 70); if (i % 30 === 5) k.tap('fire'); if (G.id === 'rocks') { if (i % 140 < 40) k.hold('thrust'); else k.up('thrust'); } }, () => [G.state(), cab.players.map(p => [p.score, p.lives])]),\n      state: () => ({ game: G.state(), stage, demo, entry: cab.entry && { name: cab.entry.name.slice(), i: cab.entry.i, score: cab.entry.score }, wheel: cab.entry && cab.wheel, continuing: cab.continuing, scores: cab.players.map(p => p.score), table: cab.table() })\n    };\n    return scene;\n  }\n  for (const G of GAMES) scenes['arcade-' + G.id] = playScene(G);\n  let showTable = null;\n  const go = i => { pick = i; A.sfx('confirm'); game.go('arcade-' + GAMES[i].id, null, { fade: 'black' }); };\n  const title = {\n    view: 'side', views: ['side'], input: KEYS, res: 'ps1', expand: true, pausable: false, touch: [], camera: { zoom: false },\n    enter(d) {\n      game.follow(null); game.cam.bounds = null; game.focus(0, 0, 0); game.cam.snap = true; A.music(SONG); L.enabled = false; game.input.consumeAll();\n      showTable = d && d.scores || null;\n      if (d && d.part && scenes['arcade-' + d.part]) game.go('arcade-' + d.part, null, { fade: 0 });   // #arcade/maze\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      const I = game.input, ph = front.attract(dt);\n      if (ph === 'demo') { const G = GAMES[demoNext++ % GAMES.length]; game.go('arcade-' + G.id, { demo: true }, { fade: 'black' }); return; }\n      if (ph !== 'scores') showTable = null; else if (!showTable) showTable = GAMES[(demoNext + GAMES.length - 1) % GAMES.length].id;\n      if (I.pressed('left')) { pick = (pick + GAMES.length - 1) % GAMES.length; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('right')) { pick = (pick + 1) % GAMES.length; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('up') || I.pressed('down')) { players = 3 - players; A.sfx('select'); }\n      if (I.pressed('confirm') || I.pressed('start') || I.pressed('fire')) { go(pick); return; }\n      const tap = I.clicked();\n      if (tap) { const i = cabsAt.findIndex(([x, y, w, h]) => tap[0] >= x && tap[0] < x + w && tap[1] >= y && tap[1] < y + h); if (i >= 0 && i < GAMES.length) go(i); else if (i === GAMES.length) { players = 3 - players; A.sfx('select'); } }\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      r.sky(['#0a0418', '#2a0a3a', '#4a1050']);\n      const t = game.time, [cw, ch] = corner(), top = touch() && r.W / 2 + 120 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) { const x = (i * 71 + t * 6 * (1 + i % 3)) % r.W, y = (i * 37) % (r.H * .7); px.dot(g, x, y, i % 5 ? '#6a5a9a' : '#ffffff'); }\n        px.rect(g, 0, r.H - 30, r.W, 30, '#1a0a26'); for (let x = 0; x < r.W; x += 16) px.rect(g, x + ((x / 16) % 2) * 8, r.H - 30, 8, 1, '#3a1a4a');\n        // the cabinets in a row, as tall as they can stand (to 1.9 times their width), centred on a tall screen\n        const n = GAMES.length, w = Math.min(84, Math.floor((r.W - 24) / n) - 8), gap = 8, x0 = Math.round(r.W / 2 - (n * w + (n - 1) * gap) / 2), hgt = Math.min(Math.round(w * 1.9), r.H - 50 - top - 70), y = Math.max(50 + top, Math.round((r.H - hgt) / 2 - 10));\n        E.font.title(g, 'ARCADE', r.W / 2, y - 40, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffffff', '#ffe040', '#ff8a40', '#ff4a8a'], depth: 3 });\n        cabsAt = [];\n        GAMES.forEach((G, i) => {   // a cabinet: a lit marquee, a screen showing the game's own picture, the control panel\n          const x = x0 + i * (w + gap), on = i === pick, sh = Math.round(hgt * .5);\n          cabsAt.push([x, y, w, hgt]);\n          px.rect(g, x, y, w, hgt, on ? '#3a2a5a' : '#221636'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 1, on ? '#8a6ac0' : '#3a2a50');\n          px.rect(g, x + 2, y + 2, w - 4, 13, G.hue[0]); px.blend(g, .3, 'add', () => px.rect(g, x + 2, y + 2, w - 4, 6, '#ffffff'));\n          E.font.text(g, G.label, x + w / 2, y + 6, '#0a0614', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n          const sx = x + 5, sy = y + 19, sw = w - 10; px.rect(g, sx, sy, sw, sh, '#000000');\n          g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(sx, sy, sw, sh); g.clip();\n          if (i === 0) { for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) px.rect(g, sx + 8 + k * 9, sy + sh / 2, 2, 2, '#ffe9a0'); const hx = sx + 6 + (t * 14) % (sw - 12); px.disc(g, hx, sy + sh / 2 + 1, 4, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, hx - 14, sy + sh / 2, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, sx, sy + 4, sw, 2, '#2a6a32'); px.rect(g, sx, sy + sh - 6, sw, 2, '#2a6a32'); }\n          if (i === 1) { for (let k = 0; k < 8; k++) px.rect(g, sx + 6 + (k % 4) * 14 + Math.sin(t * 1.5) * 4, sy + 8 + Math.floor(k / 4) * 10, 6, 4, k < 4 ? '#3ad860' : '#4a8aff'); px.rect(g, sx + sw / 2 - 2 + Math.sin(t) * 18, sy + sh - 9, 5, 5, '#f0f0f8'); px.rect(g, sx + sw / 2 + Math.sin(t) * 18, sy + sh - 18 - (t * 60) % 30, 1, 4, '#ffffff'); }\n          if (i === 2) { for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) { const cx = sx + 10 + ((k * 23 + t * 9) % (sw - 10)), cy = sy + 10 + ((k * 17 + t * 5) % (sh - 14)), R = 3 + k % 3 * 2; for (let q = 0; q < 6; q++) px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(q) * R, cy + Math.sin(q) * R, cx + Math.cos(q + 1) * R, cy + Math.sin(q + 1) * R, '#c8d8ff'); } const a = t * 1.3, cx = sx + sw / 2, cy = sy + sh / 2; px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * 5, cy + Math.sin(a) * 5, cx + Math.cos(a + 2.5) * 4, cy + Math.sin(a + 2.5) * 4, '#ffffff'); px.line(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * 5, cy + Math.sin(a) * 5, cx + Math.cos(a - 2.5) * 4, cy + Math.sin(a - 2.5) * 4, '#ffffff'); }\n          g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n          px.blend(g, .12, 'add', () => px.rect(g, sx, sy, sw, 3, '#ffffff'));\n          const py = sy + sh + 5; px.rect(g, x + 3, py, w - 6, Math.max(10, hgt - (py - y) - 14), '#140c22');\n          px.disc(g, x + 14, py + 8, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, x + 13, py + 1, 2, 7, '#c8c8d0'); px.disc(g, x + w - 22, py + 8, 3, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x + w - 12, py + 8, 3, '#4ae8ff');\n          const hi = cabs[G.id].table()[0]; E.font.text(g, 'HI ' + (hi ? hi.score : 0), x + w / 2, y + hgt - 10, '#c8b8f0', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n          if (on) { const k = Math.floor(t * 3) % 2 ? '#ffffff' : '#ffe040'; px.rect(g, x - 2, y - 2, w + 4, 2, k); px.rect(g, x - 2, y + hgt, w + 4, 2, k); px.rect(g, x - 2, y, 2, hgt, k); px.rect(g, x + w, y, 2, hgt, k); }\n        });\n        // one or two players (up and down, or a tap on it)\n        const by = y + hgt + 6, bw = 96, bh = touch() ? 34 : 16; cabsAt.push([Math.round(r.W / 2 - bw / 2), by, bw, bh]);   // (a thumb's size on a touch screen)\n        px.rect(g, r.W / 2 - bw / 2, by, bw, bh, '#2a1a3e'); E.font.text(g, players === 1 ? '< 1 PLAYER >' : '< 2 PLAYERS >', r.W / 2, by + bh / 2 - 3, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', outline: false });\n        E.font.text(g, GAMES[pick].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 22, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n        E.font.text(g, touch() ? 'TAP A CABINET TO PLAY' : game.input.lastDevice === 'gamepad' ? 'D-PAD + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   Y CLASSIC LOOK' : 'ARROWS + ENTER   C CLASSIC LOOK', r.W / 2, r.H - 11, '#9a8ac8', { align: 'center', outline: false, font: 'tiny' });\n      });\n      if (showTable) { r.overlay(g => { g.fillStyle = 'rgba(4,2,12,.88)'; g.fillRect(0, 0, r.bw, r.bh); px.reset(g); }); cabs[showTable].drawTable(r, '', Math.max(16, Math.round(r.H / 2 - 82)), GAMES.find(G => G.id === showTable).label + ' HIGH SCORES'); }\n    },\n    back() { game.go('title'); return true; },\n    /** the bot (tools/kits-test.mjs): each game played by its own demo pilot, from a seed, until it clears two stages (or\n     *  five minutes of game time, or its lives run out); then the attract mode left alone: the demo it starts, the table, the title again. What they reached */\n    bot() {\n      const was = Math.random, out = {}, A0 = game.audio.muted; Math.random = E.rng(9);\n      try {\n        for (const G of GAMES) {\n          game.time = 0; game.go('arcade-' + G.id, { demo: true }, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n          const cab = cabs[G.id]; let t = 0, cleared = 0;\n          while (t < 300 && !G.over && G.level < 3) { cab.update(1 / 120); G.step(1 / 120, game.input); t += 1 / 120; if (G.level > 1 && !cleared) cleared = Math.round(t); }\n          out[G.id] = { score: cab.players[0].score, level: G.level, cleared, lives: cab.players[0].lives, over: !!G.over, seconds: Math.round(t) };\n        }\n        game.go('arcade', null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120); front.wake();\n        game.advance(front.o.idle + .5); const demoAt = game.sceneName;\n        for (let i = 0; i < 40 && game.sceneName !== 'arcade'; i++) game.advance(1);\n        const back = game.sceneName, table = front.phase === 'scores'; game.advance(front.o.scores + .5);\n        out.attract = demoAt.startsWith('arcade-') && back === 'arcade' && table && front.phase === 'title';\n        out.errors = game.errors.length; return out;\n      } finally { Math.random = was; }\n    },\n    /** what the title shows: the game picked, one or two players, where each cabinet is (and the players button, last) on\n     *  screen, the attract mode's phase */\n    state: () => ({ pick, players, cabs: cabsAt, phase: front.phase, table: showTable }),\n    /** the proof: each game's proof, one after the other */\n    run: (n = 600) => GAMES.map(G => scenes['arcade-' + G.id].run(n)).join('-')\n  };\n  return title;\n})();\nscenes.arcade = ARCADE;\n\n/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n// a genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\nfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\ntitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n// #<slice>/<part> jumps in (#arcade/maze, #shooter/horizontal): the slice's enter(data) gets { part }; a part that is a\n// scene of its own (the slice's parts: { battle: 'rpg-battle' }) starts there\nconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: to || (sc ? first : 'title'), data: sc && part ? { part } : undefined });\nwindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu };   // for tests\n})();\n/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat vendor/hub/lib/hub/examples/arena.html && cat vendor/hub/scripts/hub-check.mjs && sed -n '1,100p' vendor/hub/lib/hub/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat vendor/hub/lib/hub/examples/arena.html && cat vendor/hub/scripts/hub-check.mjs && sed -n '1,100p' vendor/hub/lib/hub/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n  }\n\n  function own(o, k) {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\n  }\n\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n\n  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n  function json(value) {\n    try {\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };\n\n  /** Milliseconds since the synchronized start: negative during the countdown, -Infinity before start. */\n  hub.time = function () {\n    return goAt === null ? -Infinity : now() - goAt;\n  };\n\n  /** A seeded random number generator (0 ≤ n < 1), the same sequence on every device for the same label. */\n  hub.rng = function (label) {\n    var h = 2166136261;\n    var s = String(label === undefined ? '' : label);\n    for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n      h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n      h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n    }\n    return generator((hub.seed ^ h) >>> 0);\n  };\n\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\n  function finite(v) {\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n  };\n\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n  };\n\n  hub.inspect = function () {\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\n    } catch (e) {\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n    }\n  };\n\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n  if (pad) {\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[0]) > 0.2) x = pad.axes[0];\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[1]) > 0.2) y = pad.axes[1];\n    if (padNow[12]) y = -1;\n    if (padNow[13]) y = 1;\n    if (padNow[14]) x = -1;\n    if (padNow[15]) x = 1;\n  }\n  if (pointer && me) {\n    const p = toWorld(pointer);\n    const dx = p.x - me.x, dy = p.y - me.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n    if (d > 8) { x = dx / d; y = dy / d; }\n  }\n  const sprint = keys.has(' ') || !!padNow[PAD.cross] || !!padNow[7];\n  const len = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  return len > 1 ? { x: x / len, y: y / len, sprint } : { x, y, sprint };\n}\n\nfunction toWorld(e) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(), s = Math.min(r.width / W, r.height / H);\n  return { x: (e.clientX - r.left - (r.width - W * s) / 2) / s, y: (e.clientY - r.top - (r.height - H * s) / 2) / s };\n}\n\n// ---- state shared by both modes\nconst game = {\n  phase: 'title',            // title | waiting | playing | over\n  players: [],               // {id, name, color, x, y, score, gone}, drawn at x, y\n  star: { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, n: 0 },   // n numbers the stars, so a claim names the one it touched\n  rng: Math.random,\n  message: '',\n  standings: null,\n};\nlet felt = { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };   // the local stick as last read\n\nfunction place(players) {\n  players.forEach((p, i) => {\n    const a = (i / Math.max(players.length, 1)) * Math.PI * 2;\n    p.tx = p.x = W / 2 + Math.cos(a) * 200; p.ty = p.y = H / 2 + Math.sin(a) * 180;\n  });\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\n\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);\n  ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n  menu.items.forEach((item, i) => {\n    ctx.fillStyle = i === menu.at ? '#ffd34d' : '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(`${i === menu.at ? '▸ ' : ''}${item.label()}`, W / 2, 226 + i * 40);\n  });\n}\n\nconnect();\nrequestAnimationFrame(frame);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n * a game before spending a model on it, since a page this browser cannot run\n * cannot be checked here. A WebGPU-only game without WebGPU is caught even\n * when its title screen shows: it asked for an adapter, got none, and drew\n * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n * Chromium; on a machine without a GPU, SwiftShader gives such games a\n * software adapter:\n *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n *\n * Every game's pasted client is also read from disk and must be exactly a\n * released one (scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs).\n *\n * --record writes the outcome into data/overrides.json, which is how the hub\n * keeps a failing game out of sessions: a game that fails gets \"session\": \"0\"\n * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n * it) and a sessionNote naming what failed; a game that passes loses both.\n *\n * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n *         (games default to the three examples in lib/hub/examples/)\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { mkdir, readdir, readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nimport { staticHandler } from './lib/serve.mjs';\nimport { modeOf, SELF_REPORTED } from '../lib/hub/round.js';\nimport { findClients } from './lib/hub-client.mjs';\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst EXAMPLES = ['/lib/hub/examples/arena.html', '/lib/hub/examples/ghost.html', '/lib/hub/examples/parallel.html'];\nconst PAGE_MS = 300_000;\n\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst option = (name, fallback) => {\n  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n  if (at === -1) return fallback;\n  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n  return value;\n};\nconst asked = option('players', null);\nlet base = option('base', null);\nconst original = option('original', null);\nconst asJson = args.includes('--json');\nconst solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\nconst retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\nconst drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\nconst record = args.includes('--record');\n/** Extra flags for the browser, e.g. the ones that give it WebGPU where the machine can (lib/kit/README.md). */\nconst browserArgs = (option('browser-args', '') || '').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\nconst asPath = (g) => (g.startsWith('/') || /^https?:/.test(g) ? g : `/${g}`);\nconst games = args.filter((a) => !a.startsWith('--')).map(asPath);\nif (!games.length) games.push(...EXAMPLES);\n\n/**\n * The player counts to try: as asked, or by the game's mode, within the seats\n * the game takes. Parallel shares nothing, so 1 and 2 say it all.\n */\nfunction countsFor(mode, [least, most]) {\n  const list = asked ?? (mode === 'parallel' ? '1,2' : '2,3,4');\n  return list.split(',').map(Number).filter((n) => n >= 1 && n <= 4 && (asked || (n >= least && n <= most)));\n}\n\n/** The game's session mode (older tags read as today's) and its seats, from its head. */\nasync function headOf(game) {\n  try {\n    const html = await (await fetch(/^https?:/.test(game) ? game : `${base}${game}`)).text();\n    const meta = (name) => html.match(new RegExp(`<meta\\\\s+name=[\"']${name}[\"']\\\\s+content=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']`, 'i'))?.[1] ?? null;\n    const [least = 1, most = least] = (meta('hub:session-players')?.match(/\\d+/g) ?? []).map(Number);\n    return { mode: modeOf(meta('hub:session-mode')), seats: [least, most] };\n  } catch {\n    return { mode: null, seats: [1, 4] };\n  }\n}\n\nlet chromium;\ntry {\n  ({ chromium } = createRequire(import.meta.url)('playwright'));\n} catch {\n  console.error('hub-check needs Playwright: pnpm add -D playwright && pnpm exec playwright install chromium');\n  process.exit(2);\n}\n\n/**\n * Runs in every frame before its own scripts: it notes what the page asks of\n * the graphics stack, and session-mode pages are watched for dialogs and sockets.\n */\nfunction watch() {\n  // What the page asked of the graphics stack: a WebGPU adapter it never got, and\n  // no WebGL drawing instead, means this browser cannot run it (a title screen may still show).\n  const gfx = (window.__gfx = { askedForWebGPU: false, gotAdapter: false, webgl: false, twoD: false });\n  if (navigator.gpu?.requestAdapter) {\n    const ask = navigator.gpu.requestAdapter.bind(navigator.gpu);\n    Object.defineProperty(navigator.gpu, 'requestAdapter', {\n      configurable: true,\n      writable: true,\n      value: async (...a) => {\n        gfx.askedForWebGPU = true;\n        const adapter = await ask(...a);\n        if (adapter) gfx.gotAdapter = true;\n        return adapter;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n  for (const Canvas of [window.HTMLCanvasElement, window.OffscreenCanvas].filter(Boolean)) {\n    const getContext = Canvas.prototype.getContext;\n    Canvas.prototype.getContext = function (type, ...rest) {\n      const context = getContext.call(this, type, ...rest);\n      if (context && /^(webgl2?|experimental-webgl)$/.test(type)) gfx.webgl = true;\n      if (context && type === '2d') gfx.twoD = true;\n      return context;\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (!/[?&]aihub=/.test(location.search)) return;\n  const seen = (window.__hubViolations = []);\n  for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n    window[name] = () => {\n      seen.push(`${name}() called`);\n      return name === 'confirm' ? false : null;\n    };\n  }\n  for (const name of ['WebSocket', 'RTCPeerConnection', 'EventSource']) {\n    const Original = window[name];\n    if (!Original) continue;\n    window[name] = function (...a) {\n      seen.push(`${name} opened in a session (${String(a[0]).slice(0, 80)})`);\n      return new Original(...a);\n    };\n  }\n  addEventListener('error', (e) => seen.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n  addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => seen.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n}\n\nlet server = null;\nif (!base) {\n  server = createServer(staticHandler(ROOT));\n  await new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));\n  base = `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`;\n}\n\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\nconst runs = [];\ntry {\n  for (const game of games) {\n    if (drawsOnly) {\n      const report = await stillWorks(game, null, { bare: true });\n      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'draws', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  draws on its own`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    const client = await clientCheck(game);\n    if (client) {\n      runs.push({ game, players: 0, scenario: 'static', pass: client.pass, checks: [client] });\n      if (!asJson && !client.pass) console.log(`FAIL  ${game}  ✗ ${client.name} — ${client.detail}`);\n    }\n    const { mode, seats } = await headOf(game);\n    const counts = countsFor(mode, seats);\n    // A retrofit is played once, at 2 players with one leaving: nothing is shared, so that says it all.\n    const plan = retrofit && !asked ? [] : counts.map((n) => ({ n, scenario: 'standard' }));\n    const leaving = retrofit && !asked ? 2 : Math.max(2, Math.min(3, Math.max(...counts, 0)));\n    if (asked || leaving <= seats[1]) plan.push({ n: leaving, scenario: 'host-leave' });\n    // A shared world must also run on a copy with no player of its own, as a server would run it.\n    if (!retrofit && mode && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode) && (asked || (seats[0] <= 2 && seats[1] >= 2))) plan.push({ n: 2, scenario: 'server' });\n    for (const { n, scenario } of plan) {\n      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 860 } });\n      await context.addInitScript(watch);\n      const page = await context.newPage();\n      const pageErrors = [];\n      const warnings = [];\n      page.on('pageerror', (e) => pageErrors.push(e.message));\n      page.on('console', (m) => m.text().startsWith('[AIHub]') && warnings.push(m.text()));\n      const query = { game, players: n, latency: 150, jitter: 50, loss: 5, auto: 1, scenario, play: 8000 };\n      const url = `${base}/lib/hub/harness.html?${new URLSearchParams(query)}`;\n      await page.goto(url);\n      // The harness times every step itself; this only catches a page that stopped answering.\n      // Four copies of a 3D game on software WebGL can take minutes.\n      const finished = await page.waitForSelector('body[data-complete=\"true\"]', { timeout: PAGE_MS }).then(() => true, () => false);\n      const report = (await page.evaluate(() => window.__hubCheck).catch(() => null)) || { pass: false, checks: [] };\n      if (!finished) {\n        report.pass = false;\n        report.checks.push({ name: `the harness finished within ${PAGE_MS / 1000} s`, pass: false, detail: `stopped after: ${report.checks.at(-1)?.name ?? 'nothing'}` });\n      }\n      const extra = [\n        { name: 'no client warnings (oversized or too many sends, misuse)', pass: !warnings.length, detail: [...new Set(warnings)].slice(0, 4).join('; ') },\n        { name: 'harness page has no errors', pass: !pageErrors.length, detail: pageErrors.join('; ') },\n      ];\n      report.checks.push(...extra);\n      report.pass = report.pass && extra.every((c) => c.pass);\n      runs.push({ game, players: n, scenario, pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) {\n        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  ${n} players  ${scenario}`);\n        for (const c of report.checks) if (!c.pass) console.log(`        ✗ ${c.name}${c.detail ? ` — ${c.detail}` : ''}`);\n      }\n      await context.close();\n    }\n    if (solo) {\n      const report = await stillWorks(game, original && asPath(original));\n      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'alone', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) {\n        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n        for (const c of report.checks) if (!c.pass) console.log(`        ✗ ${c.name}${c.detail ? ` — ${c.detail}` : ''}`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n} finally {\n  await browser.close();\n  server?.close();\n}\n\n/** The pasted client, read from disk: one copy, exactly a released one. Null for a game served from elsewhere. */\nasync function clientCheck(game) {\n  if (/^https?:/.test(game)) return null;\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, decodeURI(game).replace(/^\\//, ''));\n  let text;\n  try {\n    text = await readFile(file, 'utf8');\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n  // A project folder may ship the client as its own file next to its page.\n  if (path.basename(file) === 'index.html' && !text.includes('aihub-session')) {\n    for (const name of await readdir(path.dirname(file)).catch(() => [])) {\n      if (/\\.m?js$/.test(name)) text += '\\n' + (await readFile(path.join(path.dirname(file), name), 'utf8').catch(() => ''));\n    }\n  }\n  const copies = findClients(text);\n  const name = 'the session client is pasted unmodified';\n  if (copies.length !== 1) return { name, pass: false, detail: `${copies.length} copies of the client` };\n  return { name, pass: copies[0].pristine, detail: copies[0].pristine ? copies[0].version : `${copies[0].version ?? 'unknown'} edited: paste lib/hub/session.js again` };\n}\n\n/**\n * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n * an original page already had), the client inactive and Math.random left\n * alone, and something drawn on the screen.\n */\nasync function stillWorks(game, before, { bare = false } = {}) {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n  const visit = async (page) => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    await context.addInitScript(watch);\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    const errors = [];\n    tab.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(e.message));\n    await tab.goto(/^https?:/.test(page) ? page : `${base}${page}`);\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2500);\n    for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\n      await tab.keyboard.press(key).catch(() => {});\n      await tab.waitForTimeout(500);\n    }\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2000);\n    const hub = await tab.evaluate(() => (window.AIHub ? { active: window.AIHub.active, seeded: window.AIHub.seeded } : null)).catch(() => null);\n    const gfx = await tab.evaluate(() => window.__gfx ?? null).catch(() => null);\n    // A WebGL or WebGPU canvas often reads back blank from a script, so look at the screen instead:\n    // a blank one compresses to almost nothing, so a PNG past a blank page's size means something is drawn.\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' }).catch(() => Buffer.alloc(0))).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return { errors, hub, bytes, gfx };\n  };\n  const blank = await (async () => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    await tab.setContent('<body style=\"margin:0;background:#000\"></body>');\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' })).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return bytes;\n  })();\n  const after = await visit(game);\n  // A line of text on a plain screen already adds about 2 KB; a uniform screen of any colour adds nothing.\n  after.drawn = after.bytes > blank + 1200;\n  const known = before ? new Set((await visit(before)).errors) : new Set();\n  const fresh = after.errors.filter((e) => !known.has(e));\n  if (!bare) {\n    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n    // A client before 1.3.0 has no seeded flag: it never seeds.\n    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n  }\n  const g = after.gfx;\n  const noWebGPU = g?.askedForWebGPU && !g.gotAdapter && !g.webgl && !g.twoD;\n  const asked = g ? `WebGPU ${g.askedForWebGPU ? (g.gotAdapter ? 'asked, adapter' : 'asked, no adapter') : 'not asked'}; WebGL ${g.webgl ? 'yes' : 'no'}; 2D ${g.twoD ? 'yes' : 'no'}` : 'not seen';\n  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n  // Drawing is all a bare page is asked: its own errors are the original's business.\n  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n  return { pass: checks.every((c) => c.pass), checks };\n}\n\n/**\n * Keep the verdict with the game: a failure takes it out of sessions until it\n * passes again (see the header). Games are found by path in data/games.json.\n */\nasync function recordChecks() {\n  let manifest;\n  try {\n    manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(ROOT, 'data/games.json'), 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    console.log('--record needs data/games.json: run pnpm scan first');\n    return;\n  }\n  const slugOf = new Map();\n  for (const g of manifest.games) for (const p of [g.path, ...(g.builds || []).map((b) => b.path)]) if (p) slugOf.set(decodeURI(p), g.slug);\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, 'data/overrides.json');\n  const overrides = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, 'utf8'));\n  const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n  for (const game of games) {\n    const slug = slugOf.get(decodeURI(game));\n    if (!slug) {\n      console.log(`--record: ${game} is not in the catalogue, nothing recorded`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    // A shared world that cannot yet be hosted by a server still plays: that run is reported, not held against it.\n    const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.game === game && r.scenario !== 'server');\n    const failed = [...new Set(mine.flatMap((r) => r.checks.filter((c) => !c.pass).map((c) => c.name)))];\n    const entry = { ...(overrides[slug] || {}) };\n    if (!failed.length) {\n      if (entry.session === '0') delete entry.session;\n      delete entry.sessionNote;\n    } else {\n      entry.session = '0';\n      entry.sessionNote = `hub-check failed on ${today}: ${failed.slice(0, 3).join('; ')}`.slice(0, 240);\n    }\n    if (Object.keys(entry).length) overrides[slug] = entry;\n    else delete overrides[slug];\n    console.log(`--record: ${slug} ${failed.length ? 'kept out of sessions' : 'may be dealt'}`);\n  }\n  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(overrides, null, 2)}\\n`);\n}\n\nconst pass = runs.every((r) => r.pass);\nif (record) await recordChecks();\nawait mkdir(path.join(ROOT, '.cache'), { recursive: true });\nawait writeFile(path.join(ROOT, '.cache', 'hub-check.json'), JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, base, pass, runs }, null, 2));\nif (asJson) console.log(JSON.stringify({ pass, runs }, null, 2));\nelse console.log(`\\n${pass ? 'All checks passed' : 'Some checks failed'} — report in .cache/hub-check.json`);\nprocess.exit(pass ? 0 : 1);\n# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card, longer if one asks for more time: what\n   the game is, how to win, the controls. The card is the hub's, from the\n   game's tags, or the game's own (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'MAZE|GridMover|Grid\\\\(|Menu\\\\(|Shell\\\\(|Arcade|maze\\\\(' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js && sed -n '180,380p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'MAZE|GridMover|Grid\\\\(|Menu\\\\(|Shell\\\\(|Arcade|maze\\\\(' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js && sed -n '180,380p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"110:const menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\n145:const overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\n162: * (C, a pad's Y, or Settings: Arcade, Look), each with its own high-score table, initials on a letter wheel, a continue,\n164: *   MAZE (#arcade/maze): eat every glow-seed in a hedge maze while four wisps hunt you, each its own way (one chases, one\n176: * HOW IT WORKS: E.Arcade (the arcade module) keeps the scores, lives, turns, tables, initials, cards, the continue and the\n177: * attract mode; the maze is an E.Grid with E.GridMovers (a turn asked early is kept), each game a { begin, step, draw }.\n182:  game.settings.define({ key: 'arcadeLook', group: 'Arcade', label: 'Look', options: [['remaster', 'Remaster'], ['classic', 'Classic']], value: 'remaster', help: 'Remaster: lit, with HD rigs and glowi [... omitted end of long line]\n224:  /* =================================== 1. MAZE =================================== */\n225:  const MAZE = (() => {\n235:      const half = E.gen.maze(15, MH, { seed: 7 + level * 13, braid: 1 }).rows;\n241:      grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' });       // yours\n242:      wgrid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] !== '#' });      // the wisps' (the house too: openFor says when)\n250:      hero = { m: new E.GridMover({ cx: start[0], cy: start[1], speed: 7.5 }), dir: [-1, 0], chomp: 0, dying: 0 };\n253:      wisps = WCOL.map((c, i) => ({ i, c, m: new E.GridMover({ cx: i ? 10 + i * 2 : DOOR[0], cy: i ? HY + 2 : DOOR[1], speed: 6.8 }), home: i > 0, wait: i * 2.5, eyes: false, leaving: false, blue: fal [... omitted end of long line]\n313:      if (!seeds.size && !power.size) { level++; cab.card('MAZE ' + level, 2); A.sfx('oneup'); if (level === 2 && !demo) intermission(); build(); reset(); readyT = 2.2; }\n416:      id: 'maze', label: 'MAZE', res: [232, 270], about: 'EAT EVERY SEED, DODGE FOUR WISPS', hue: ['#ffe040', '#4ae8ff', '#ff4a8a'], touch: [], extra: [10000], light: .5,\n632:  const GAMES = [MAZE, FORM, ROCKS];\n633:  const cabs = {}; for (const G of GAMES) cabs[G.id] = new E.Arcade(game, { id: G.id, lives: 3, extra: G.extra || [], every: G.every });\n634:  const front = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'arcade', idle: 20, demo: 1e9, scores: 6 });   // the title's attract clock (a demo ends itself: endDemo)\n  const KEYS = Object.assign({}, E.Input.SHMUP, { thrust: ['Pad2', 'Pad5'], warp: ['KeyX', 'KeyK', 'ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1', 'Pad6'], classic: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'] });\n  delete KEYS.bomb;\n  game.settings.define({ key: 'arcadeLook', group: 'Arcade', label: 'Look', options: [['remaster', 'Remaster'], ['classic', 'Classic']], value: 'remaster', help: 'Remaster: lit, with HD rigs and glowing lines. Classic: as the cabinets first looked. C switches it in play' });\n  const classic = () => game.settings.arcadeLook === 'classic';\n  // the cabinet's own tune (the step sequencer's format): A minor, a bouncing bass\n  const SONG = { bpm: 132, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .12, notes: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . A5 - G5 . E5 . C5 . D5 . | E5 - - . D5 . C5 . B4 . G4 . A4 - - . | F4 . A4 . C5 . F5 - E5 . C5 . A4 . B4 . | C5 . B4 . A4 . G#4 . A4 - - - - . . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 . | C3 . C4 . C3 . C4 . G2 . G3 . G2 . G3 . | F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . F2 . F3 . | E2 . E3 . E2 . E3 . A2 . A3 . A2 . A3 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .12, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h h' }] };\n  // the remaster's deep space (the classic look keeps plain black): a planet, nebulae drifting, many stars\n  const SPACE = [['#020208', '#0a0a24', '#1a0c30', '#2a1038'], ['#02040a', '#06142a', '#0c1c3a', '#1a1a3a']].map((sky, i) => new E.Backdrop({ sky, moon: { x: i ? .16 : .82, y: i ? .7 : .22, r: i ? 22 : 15, color: i ? '#8ab0d8' : '#b89ae8' }, stars: 140,\n    layers: [{ kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#1a4a6a' : '#6a3aa8', y: .3, height: .45, parallax: .03, drift: 1, nebula: true, seed: 2 + i }, { kind: 'clouds', color: i ? '#3a2a5a' : '#2a5ab0', y: .72, height: .4, parallax: .05, drift: 2, nebula: true, seed: 5 + i }] }));\n  // cabinet art round a playfield of one fixed screen: on a wide screen's sides (left of x0, right of x1) a lit bezel edge,\n  // a marquee stripe and drifting sparks; on a tall one (above y0, below y1) the marquee with the game's name and the\n  // control panel\n  function cabinet(r, x0, x1, hue, y0 = 0, y1 = r.H, label = '') {\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      const H = r.H, t = game.time;\n      if (y0 > 40) {\n        px.rect(g, 0, 0, r.W, y0 - 4, '#0a0614'); px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 34, hue[0]); px.blend(g, .25, 'add', () => px.rect(g, 8, y0 - 46, r.W - 16, 12, '#ffffff'));\n        E.font.title(g, label, r.W / 2, y0 - 42, { align: 'center', scale: 2, colors: ['#ffffff', '#1a1030'], depth: 1 });\n      }\n      if (H - y1 > 40) {\n        const y = y1 + 6; px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, H - y, '#140c22'); px.rect(g, 0, y, r.W, 2, hue[0]);\n        const cy = y + Math.min(40, (H - y) / 2); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy, 8, '#2a1a3e'); px.rect(g, r.W / 2 - 51, cy - 16, 3, 16, '#c8c8d0'); px.disc(g, r.W / 2 - 50, cy - 17, 5, '#ff4a4a');\n        for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.disc(g, r.W / 2 + 10 + i * 18, cy, 6, hue[i]);\n      }\n      for (const [a, b, right] of [[0, x0, false], [x1, r.W, true]]) {\n        if (b - a < 3) continue;\n        // the side's art: a dark panel tinted toward the game's colour, lit stripes slanting across it\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) px.rect(g, a, Math.floor(H * i / 8), b - a, Math.ceil(H / 8) + 1, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .03 + i * .018));\n        g.save(); g.beginPath(); g.rect(a, 0, b - a, H); g.clip();\n        for (let x = a - H; x < b + 40; x += 46) { const k = right ? 1 : -1, x1 = right ? x : b - (x - a); px.blend(g, .1, 'add', () => px.poly(g, [[x1, 0], [x1 + 18 * k, 0], [x1 + 18 * k + H * .5 * k, H], [x1 + H * .5 * k, H]], hue[1])); }\n        const sw = (y0, y1, c) => px.poly(g, right ? [[a, H * y0], [b, H * (y0 - .3)], [b, H * (y1 - .3)], [a, H * y1]] : [[b, H * y0], [a, H * (y0 - .3)], [a, H * (y1 - .3)], [b, H * y1]], c);\n        sw(.5, .74, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[0], .7)); sw(.5, .52, '#ffffff'); sw(.76, .8, E.mix('#0a0614', hue[1], .8));   // a swoosh in the game's colours\n        g.restore(); px.reset(g);\n        if (label && b - a >= 44) { const n = label.length, k = Math.min(4, Math.floor((H - 20) / n / 9)), y0 = Math.round(H / 2 - n * k * 4.5); for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) E.font.title(g, label[i], (a + b) / 2, y0 + i * k * 9, { align: 'center', scale: k, colors: ['#ffffff', E.shade(hue[0], .3), hue[0]], depth: 2 }); }   // the game's name down the side\n        for (let y = -24; y < H; y += 24) { const yy = Math.round(y + (t * 20) % 24); px.rect(g, right ? a + 6 : b - 10, yy, 4, 12, hue[1]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 14 : b - 18, yy + 12, 2, 6, hue[2]); }\n        for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) { const y = (i * 61 + t * (12 + i * 3)) % (H + 20) - 10, x = right ? a + 10 + (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14) : b - 10 - (i * 13) % Math.max(8, b - a - 14); px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, x, y, 1 + i % 3, hue[i % 3])); }\n        px.rect(g, right ? a : b - 3, 0, 3, H, hue[0]); px.rect(g, right ? a + 3 : b - 4, 0, 1, H, '#ffffff');\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  /* =================================== 1. MAZE =================================== */\n  const MAZE = (() => {\n    const C8 = 8, MW = 29, MH = 31, TUN = 17, HX = 10, HY = 11, DOOR = [14, 10], WCOL = ['#ff4a4a', '#ff9ad8', '#4ae8ff', '#ffb84a'];\n    const CORNER = [[MW - 2, -3], [1, -3], [MW - 1, MH], [0, MH]], PHASES = [7, 20, 7, 20, 5, 20, 5, 1e9], WAYS = [[0, -1], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0]];   // (up, left, down, right: the original's order for ties)\n    let cells, grid, wgrid, start, seeds, power, hero = null, wisps = null, mode, modeT, phase, fright, eaten, level, cab, demo, over, deathT, readyT, inter, berry, ate, X0 = 0, Y0 = 12;\n    const key = (x, y) => x + ',' + y, cellOf = k => k.split(',').map(Number);\n    const nearest = (x, y, ok) => { let best = [x, y], bd = 1e9; for (let b = 0; b < MH; b++) for (let a = 0; a < MW; a++) if (ok(a, b)) { const d = Math.abs(a - x) + Math.abs(b - y); if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = [a, b]; } } return best; };\n    const ring = (x, y) => y >= HY - 1 && y <= HY + 5 && x >= HX - 1 && x <= HX + 9;\n    // a new maze: the left half from E.gen's braided maze, mirrored; doors in the middle wall; the wisps' house in a ring\n    // of hall; the tunnel's ends opened. The same level gives the same maze\n    function build() {\n      const half = E.gen.maze(15, MH, { seed: 7 + level * 13, braid: 1 }).rows;\n      cells = half.map(r => (r + r.slice(0, 14).split('').reverse().join('')).split(''));\n      for (let y = 1; y < MH - 1; y += 4) if (cells[y][13] === '.') cells[y][14] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY - 1; y <= HY + 5; y++) for (let x = HX - 1; x <= HX + 9; x++) cells[y][x] = '.';\n      for (let y = HY; y <= HY + 4; y++) for (let x = HX; x <= HX + 8; x++) cells[y][x] = y === HY || y === HY + 4 || x === HX || x === HX + 8 ? '#' : 'H';\n      cells[HY][14] = '-'; cells[TUN][0] = cells[TUN][MW - 1] = '.';\n      grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' });       // yours\n      wgrid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => cells[y][x] !== '#' });      // the wisps' (the house too: openFor says when)\n      start = nearest(14, 23, (x, y) => cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y));\n      seeds = new Set(); power = new Set(); ate = 0; berry = null;\n      for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 1; x < MW - 1; x++) if (cells[y][x] === '.' && !ring(x, y) && !(x === start[0] && y === start[1])) seeds.add(key(x, y));\n      for (const [x, y] of [[1, 3], [MW - 2, 3], [1, MH - 4], [MW - 2, MH - 4]]) { const k = key(...nearest(x, y, (a, b) => seeds.has(key(a, b)))); seeds.delete(k); power.add(k); }\n    }\n    // everyone to their places: you below the house, the first wisp at its door, the others inside waiting their turn\n    function reset() {\n      hero = { m: new E.GridMover({ cx: start[0], cy: start[1], speed: 7.5 }), dir: [-1, 0], chomp: 0, dying: 0 };\n      hero.m.dir = [-1, 0];\n      const was = wisps;\n      wisps = WCOL.map((c, i) => ({ i, c, m: new E.GridMover({ cx: i ? 10 + i * 2 : DOOR[0], cy: i ? HY + 2 : DOOR[1], speed: 6.8 }), home: i > 0, wait: i * 2.5, eyes: false, leaving: false, blue: false,\n        rig: was ? was[i].rig : new E.Blob({ R: 3.6, face: 'front', colors: { dk: E.shade(c, -.35), base: c, lt: E.shade(c, .35) } }) }));\n      for (const w of wisps) w.m.dir = [w.i % 2 ? 1 : -1, 0];\n      mode = 'scatter'; modeT = 0; phase = 0; fright = 0; eaten = 0; readyT = 1.8; deathT = 0;\n    }\n    // where each aims while chasing: at you; four cells ahead of you; past a point two ahead, as far again as the first wisp\n    // is behind it (they pincer); at you from afar, its corner up close. Scattering: its corner. Eyes and leavers: the door\n    function target(w) {\n      if (w.eyes || w.leaving) return DOOR;\n      if (mode === 'scatter') return CORNER[w.i];\n      const h = hero.m, [dx, dy] = hero.dir;\n      if (w.i === 0) return [h.cx, h.cy];\n      if (w.i === 1) return [h.cx + dx * 4, h.cy + dy * 4];\n      if (w.i === 2) { const a = wisps[0].m; return [(h.cx + dx * 2) * 2 - a.cx, (h.cy + dy * 2) * 2 - a.cy]; }\n      return Math.hypot(w.m.cx - h.cx, w.m.cy - h.cy) > 8 ? [h.cx, h.cy] : CORNER[3];\n    }\n    const openFor = (w, x, y) => { if (x < 0 || x >= MW) return y === TUN; const c = cells[y] && cells[y][x]; return c === '.' || ((c === 'H' || c === '-') && (w.eyes || w.leaving)); };\n    // at each cell a wisp takes the open way (never straight back) nearest its target; blue, a random one; eyes, the\n    // grid's path home\n    function choose(w) {\n      const m = w.m;\n      if (w.eyes) { const p = grid.path([m.cx, m.cy], DOOR); if (p.length > 1) return [p[1][0] - m.cx, p[1][1] - m.cy]; }\n      const ways = WAYS.filter(([a, b]) => !(a === -m.dir[0] && b === -m.dir[1]) && openFor(w, m.cx + a, m.cy + b));\n      if (!ways.length) return [-m.dir[0], -m.dir[1]];\n      if (w.blue) return ways[Math.floor(Math.random() * ways.length)];\n      const t = target(w), d = c => (m.cx + c[0] - t[0]) ** 2 + (m.cy + c[1] - t[1]) ** 2;\n      return ways.reduce((p, q) => d(q) < d(p) ? q : p);\n    }\n    // the tunnel: off one end, on at the other, going the same way\n    function wrapTunnel(m) { if (m.cy !== TUN || m.moving) return; if (m.cx === 0 && m.dir[0] < 0) { m.place(MW - 1, TUN); m.dir = [-1, 0]; } else if (m.cx === MW - 1 && m.dir[0] > 0) { m.place(0, TUN); m.dir = [1, 0]; } }\n    const dirOf = v => Math.hypot(v[0], v[1]) < .4 ? null : Math.abs(v[0]) > Math.abs(v[1]) ? [Math.sign(v[0]), 0] : [0, Math.sign(v[1])];\n    const pos = m => ({ x: X0 + (m.x + .5) * C8, y: Y0 + (m.y + .5) * C8 });\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      if (inter) return;   // (the intermission is a script: it moves its own actors)\n      if (readyT > 0) { readyT -= dt; return; }\n      const h = hero.m;\n      if (deathT > 0) { hero.dying = deathT; if ((deathT -= dt) <= 0) lost(); return; }\n      if (fright > 0) { if ((fright -= dt) <= 0) for (const w of wisps) w.blue = false; }\n      else if ((modeT += dt) > PHASES[phase]) { modeT = 0; phase = Math.min(PHASES.length - 1, phase + 1); mode = phase % 2 ? 'chase' : 'scatter'; }\n      // you: the stick's way, kept until it can be taken (a turn asked early), going on until a wall\n      h.update(dt, grid, demo ? botDir() : dirOf(I.move()), { keep: true });\n      if (h.moving) hero.dir = h.dir;\n      wrapTunnel(h); hero.chomp = Math.max(0, hero.chomp - dt);\n      const k = key(h.cx, h.cy);\n      if (seeds.delete(k)) { cab.add(10); ate++; hero.chomp = .25; A.sfx('blip', { vol: .25, pitch: ate % 2 ? 1 : 1.2 }); if (ate === 70 || ate === 170) berry = { t: 9 }; }\n      if (power.delete(k)) { cab.add(50); fright = Math.max(1.5, 7 - level); eaten = 0; for (const w of wisps) w.blue = !w.eyes; A.sfx('powerup'); P.ring(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 2, 30, '#ffd060', .4); }\n      if (berry && (berry.t -= dt) <= 0) berry = null;\n      if (berry && h.cx === 14 && h.cy === TUN) { cab.add(100 * level, pos(h)); berry = null; A.sfx('pickup'); P.glints(pos(h).x, pos(h).y, 4, 6, '#ff8a8a'); }\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const m = w.m;\n        if (w.home) { if ((w.wait -= dt) > 0) { m.y = HY + 2 + Math.sin(game.time * 6 + w.i) * .3; continue; } w.home = false; w.leaving = true; m.y = m.cy; }\n        m.speed = w.eyes ? 15 : w.blue ? 4.2 : m.cy === TUN && (m.cx < 5 || m.cx > MW - 6) ? 4 : 6.6 + level * .25;\n        m.update(dt, wgrid, m.moving ? null : choose(w), { blocked: (x, y) => !openFor(w, x, y) });\n        wrapTunnel(m);\n        if (!m.moving && m.cx === DOOR[0] && m.cy === DOOR[1]) { w.leaving = false; if (w.eyes) { w.eyes = false; w.blue = false; } }\n        if (!w.eyes && Math.abs(m.x - h.x) + Math.abs(m.y - h.y) < .8) {\n          if (w.blue) { w.eyes = true; w.blue = false; eaten++; cab.add(200 * 2 ** (eaten - 1), pos(m)); A.sfx('kick'); game.freeze(.3); P.sparks(pos(m).x, pos(m).y, 2, 8); }\n          else { deathT = 1.5; A.sfx('die'); return; }\n        }\n      }\n      if (!seeds.size && !power.size) { level++; cab.card('MAZE ' + level, 2); A.sfx('oneup'); if (level === 2 && !demo) intermission(); build(); reset(); readyT = 2.2; }\n    }\n    // after the death's turn: a life gone; the other player's maze (two players, each keeps theirs), or the end\n    function lost() {\n      const was = cab.p, r = cab.die();\n      if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; }\n      if (r === 'next') { was.save = { level, seeds, power, ate }; const s = cab.p.save; level = s ? s.level : 1; build(); if (s) ({ seeds, power, ate } = s); }\n      reset();\n    }\n    // the intermission (a script): a wisp chases you across, then you come back big and chase it\n    function intermission() {\n      const a = { x: -30, big: false }; inter = a;\n      game.script(function* () { yield game.tween(a, { x: MW * C8 + 40 }, 2.6, { ease: 'linear' }); a.big = true; yield .4; yield game.tween(a, { x: -60 }, 2.2, { ease: 'linear' }); yield .3; inter = null; });\n    }\n    // the demo's player (the attract mode, and tools/kits-test.mjs): it counts the steps to every cell, its own and the\n    // wisps' (breadth first, through the tunnel); a cell is safe when it gets there two steps before any of them. It goes\n    // the safe way to the nearest seed (a lantern when they close in, a blue wisp while there is time), else to the\n    // neighbour they reach last\n    function steps(from, ok) {\n      const D = new Map(), up = new Map(); let q = [];\n      for (const [c, d] of from) { const k = key(...c); if (!D.has(k) || D.get(k) > d) { D.set(k, d); q.push(c); } }\n      while (q.length) {\n        const n = [];\n        for (const c of q) { const d = D.get(key(...c)); for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = c[0] + a; const y = c[1] + b; if (y === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; const k = key(x, y); if (!grid.walk([x, y]) || D.has(k) || (ok && !ok(x, y, d + 1))) continue; D.set(k, d + 1); up.set(k, c); n.push([x, y]); } }\n        q = n;\n      }\n      return { D, up };\n    }\n    function botDir() {\n      const h = hero.m; if (h.moving) return null;\n      const src = [];\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        if (w.eyes || w.blue) continue;\n        if (w.home || w.leaving) { if (!w.home || w.wait < 2) src.push([DOOR, w.home ? 3 : 1]); continue; }\n        src.push([[w.m.cx, w.m.cy], 0]); const n = [w.m.cx + w.m.dir[0], w.m.cy + w.m.dir[1]]; if (grid.walk(n)) src.push([n, 0]);\n      }\n      const W = steps(src).D, wd = (x, y) => W.has(key(x, y)) ? W.get(key(x, y)) : 99, safe = (x, y, d) => d + 2 < wd(x, y);\n      const S = steps([[[h.cx, h.cy], 0]], safe), near = wd(h.cx, h.cy) < 7;\n      const goals = fright > 2.5 && wisps.some(w => w.blue) ? wisps.filter(w => w.blue).map(w => key(w.m.cx, w.m.cy)) : near && [...power].some(k => S.D.has(k)) ? [...power] : [...seeds, ...power];\n      let best = null, bd = 1e9; for (const k of goals) { const d = S.D.get(k); if (d > 0 && d < bd) { bd = d; best = k; } }\n      if (best) { let c = cellOf(best), p; while ((p = S.up.get(key(...c))) && !(p[0] === h.cx && p[1] === h.cy)) c = p; return [Math.sign(E.wrapDiff(h.cx, c[0], MW)), c[1] - h.cy]; }\n      let far = null, fd = -1;\n      for (const [a, b] of WAYS) { let x = h.cx + a; if (h.cy === TUN) x = (x + MW) % MW; if (grid.walk([x, h.cy + b]) && wd(x, h.cy + b) > fd) { fd = wd(x, h.cy + b); far = [a, b]; } }\n      return far;\n    }\n    function layout() { X0 = Math.round((game.W - MW * C8) / 2); Y0 = Math.max(12, Math.round((game.H - MH * C8) / 2)); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), t = game.time, [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), bx = ox + X0, by = oy + Y0;\n      r.sky(cl ? ['#000000', '#000000'] : ['#04030c', '#0a0820', '#120a28']);\n      // the maze on the floor (lit in the remaster: hedges with a sunlit top edge and a shadow at the foot; the classic's\n      // thin blue lines facing the halls)\n      r.decal(g => {\n        const wall = (x, y) => !!cells[y] && cells[y][x] === '#';\n        for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n          const c = cells[y][x], X = bx + x * C8, Y = by + y * C8;\n          if (c === '#') {\n            if (cl) { px.col(g, '#2121de'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + 2, C8, 1); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + C8 - 3, C8, 1); if (!wall(x - 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + 2, Y, 1, C8); if (!wall(x + 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + C8 - 3, Y, 1, C8); }\n            else { px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, '#1c4a22'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, 2, '#5aa84a'); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y + C8 - 2, C8, 2, '#0c2410'); if (E.hash2(x, y) < .3) px.dot(g, X + 2 + (x * 3) % 4, Y + 3 + (y * 5) % 3, '#7ac860'); }\n          } else if (c === '-') px.rect(g, X, Y + 3, C8, 2, cl ? '#ffb8ff' : '#e0a0ff');\n          else if (!cl) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, (x + y) % 2 ? '#141026' : '#171230');\n        }\n      });\n      // the seeds, lanterns and the berry: glowing (they stay bright under the light)\n      r.queue(0, -1e4, 0, g => {\n        for (const k of seeds) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 3, Y = by + y * C8 + 3; px.rect(g, X, Y, 2, 2, cl ? '#ffb897' : '#ffe9a0'); if (!cl) px.dot(g, X, Y, '#ffffff'); }\n        if (Math.floor(t * 4) % 2 || readyT > 0) for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 4, Y = by + y * C8 + 4; if (cl) px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#ffb897'); else { px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, X, Y, 6, '#ffb030')); px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#fff4c0'); } }\n        if (berry) { const X = bx + 14 * C8 + 4, Y = by + TUN * C8 + 4; px.disc(g, X - 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.disc(g, X + 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.dot(g, X - 2, Y, '#ffb0b0'); px.rect(g, X - 1, Y - 3, 3, 1, '#4ad84a'); }\n      }, { emissive: true, bias: -1e6 });\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
