ilures.append(name + (': ' + str(detail) if detail else ''))\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=['--no-sandbox'])\n    try:\n        ctx = browser.new_context(viewport={'width':1920,'height':1080})\n        page = ctx.new_page()\n        errors=[]\n        page.on('pageerror', lambda e: errors.append(str(e)))\n        page.goto(ARTIFACT.as_uri()+'?test=1')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.game && window.mix', timeout=20000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1200)\n        check('direct-file title boots', page.evaluate('mix.screen === \\\"title\\\" && \"'!AIHub.active'\"'))\n        check('default music is ten percent', page.evaluate('game.settings.music === .1 && game.audio.musicVolume === .1'))\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'title-tv.png'))\n        page.get_by_role('button',name='Play solo',exact=True).click()\n        page.wait_for_function('mix.screen === \\\"play\\\"', timeout=10000)\n        page.wait_for_timeout(2900)\n        page.keyboard.down('KeyD')\n        page.wait_for_timeout(650)\n        page.keyboard.up('KeyD')\n        check('keyboard legal movement changes position', page.evaluate('mix.world.players[0].m.x > 2'))\n        page.screenshot(path=str(OUT/'play-tv.png'))\n        check('engine captured no errors', page.evaluate('game.errors.length === 0'), page.evaluate('game.errors.map(e=>e.message)'))\n        check('browser raised no errors',not errors,errors)\n        details['state']=page.evaluate('({screen:mix.screen,menu:mix.ui.screen,errors:game.errors.map(e=>e.message),player:mix.world.players[0].m.x})')\n        ctx.close()\n    except Exception as e:\n        check('browser suite completed',False,str(e))\n    finally:\n        browser.close()\nprint(json.dumps({'passed':passed,'failed':failed,'skipped':0,'failures':failures,'details':details}))\nEOF\nnode tools/test.mjs --unit --smoke\"","aggregated_output":"8 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Issue ledger\n\nOnly unique issues found by verification count here. Counts are finalized after release checks.\n\n| ID | Severity | Caught by | Finding | Fix / verification |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I01 | Major balance | First legal-input campaign trace | Snacks followed random goals too passively; the full solo campaign cleared in 120 seconds and many boards ended before feature exploration. | Strengthened committed fleeing at junctions, retained no-reversal policy and small turn tells; legal traces now take longer and use route cuts. Broader timing samples pending. |\n\nFocused code review also corrected seam reversal coordinate representation and numeric seed re-hashing before the browser/net suites; these are recorded design corrections, not extra claimed testing findings.\nEOF\ncat > docs/coverage.md <<'EOF'\n# Mechanic and stage coverage\n\n| Mechanic | Playable location | Verification |\n|---|---|---|\n| Twelve moving foods / acceleration / interception | All six, remix, custom | Legal-intent solo/co-op campaigns; movement and food invariants |\n| Follower, interceptor, keeper and power chain | All six | Predator state/chain boundary checks; normal campaigns |\n| Explicit paired tunnels | Stages 2, 3, 5, 6 | Seam motion/encounters; graph paths; normal input trace |\n| Single opening / quarter-turn pen / safe occupancy | Stages 3–6; optional custom | All-state graph validation; occupied-gate deferral and shortcut measurement |\n| Invisible walls, collision echo, reveal chirp | Stages 4 and 6; remix/custom options | Cooldown/reveal checks; targeted visual inspection |\n| Seed reproducibility / fallback | Stage 5, Remix | Bounded seed sample, equality and connectedness checks |\n| Five lives, respawn, clear restore, last-bite grace | Every run | Swept contact and lifecycle boundary checks |\n| Six-stage finale and retry | Campaign | Whole-campaign legal intents, browser results/retry |\n| Shared simultaneous play | Couch duo and AI Hub | Two-seat legal trace; official harness including dedicated host; real-state packet repair |\n| Workshop edit/save/load/code/play/return | Maze workshop | Roundtrip and invalid-code rejection checks |\n| Attract, live dev sliders, all settings/credits | Title at ten seconds; Pause | Browser input/device, idle isolation, tuning/reset checks |\n| Procedural score / SFX / gibberish | All gameplay | Web Audio/offline signal tests; defaults/mute/end checks |\nEOF\ncat > docs/authoring.md <<'EOF'\n# Adding a maze\n\nAdd a version 1 stage object to src/content/stages.js. All stages use 21 × 17 rows of # walls and . floor; two hero spawns, twelve uniquely numbered f0–f11 foods (eight ordinary/four starred), three personality definitions inside the centred pen, paired horizontal tunnels, gate and reveal presets, introduction/clear copy, seed and stable ID. The existing authored corridor segment lists are editable data, not AI branches.\n\nKeep the 5 × 5 permanent pen at x8–12/y6–10, its 3 × 3 interior, four possible door cells, and an exterior connected ring. The door is a graph state, never a decorative-only wall. Set gate.turning to introduce rotations. Reveal kind is none, all, or bands; the latter fades only upper/lower sections. Predators have data-driven release times and speed multipliers.\n\nM.validate reports actionable errors and cells: dimensions/types, boundaries, paired tunnel rows, food identity/type counts, distinct spawns, permanent pen, three roles, safe two-exit pockets, all-orientation reachability and at least six interception loops. Do not bypass it. Test a new board with legal-intent Bot and ordinary lives/speed, then use actual controls and view its last-three-food phase.\n\nThe Maze workshop exports {format:\\\"mix-up-maze\\\",version:1,board:...}. Import uses the same validator and retains the existing maze on error. Saves use a versioned profile with three slots; native engine settings have their own versioned schema. Invalid/unavailable storage falls back to visit memory with a notice.\n\nCustom shapes/materials live in view/theatre.js and extend E.SHAPES/E.MATERIALS. Creatures derive from E.Blob; their authoritative states drive their look, feet, squash, mouths and tells. Audio data/instruments live in audio/sound.js. Neither art nor audio draws gameplay randomness.\n\nBuild with npm run build. Test with npm test; targeted iterations use node tools/test.mjs --unit, --browser, or --hub. Open the HTML beside the development directory directly. No runtime resource fetches or CDN dependencies are required.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Issue ledger\n\nOnly unique issues found by verification count here. Counts are finalized after release checks.\n\n| ID | Severity | Caught by | Finding | Fix / verification |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I01 | Major balance | First legal-input campaign trace | Snacks followed random goals too passively; the full solo campaign cleared in 120 seconds and many boards ended before feature exploration. | Strengthened committed fleeing at junctions, retained no-reversal policy and small turn tells; legal traces now take longer and use route cuts. Broader timing samples pending. |\n\nFocused code review also corrected seam reversal coordinate representation and numeric seed re-hashing before the browser/net suites; these are recorded design corrections, not extra claimed testing findings.\nEOF\ncat > docs/coverage.md <<'EOF'\n# Mechanic and stage coverage\n\n| Mechanic | Playable location | Verification |\n|---|---|---|\n| Twelve moving foods / acceleration / interception | All six, remix, custom | Legal-intent solo/co-op campaigns; movement and food invariants |\n| Follower, interceptor, keeper and power chain | All six | Predator state/chain boundary checks; normal campaigns |\n| Explicit paired tunnels | Stages 2, 3, 5, 6 | Seam motion/encounters; graph paths; normal input trace |\n| Single opening / quarter-turn pen / safe occupancy | Stages 3–6; optional custom | All-state graph validation; occupied-gate deferral and shortcut measurement |\n| Invisible walls, collision echo, reveal chirp | Stages 4 and 6; remix/custom options | Cooldown/reveal checks; targeted visual inspection |\n| Seed reproducibility / fallback | Stage 5, Remix | Bounded seed sample, equality and connectedness checks |\n| Five lives, respawn, clear restore, last-bite grace | Every run | Swept contact and lifecycle boundary checks |\n| Six-stage finale and retry | Campaign | Whole-campaign legal intents, browser results/retry |\n| Shared simultaneous play | Couch duo and AI Hub | Two-seat legal trace; official harness including dedicated host; real-state packet repair |\n| Workshop edit/save/load/code/play/return | Maze workshop | Roundtrip and invalid-code rejection checks |\n| Attract, live dev sliders, all settings/credits | Title at ten seconds; Pause | Browser input/device, idle isolation, tuning/reset checks |\n| Procedural score / SFX / gibberish | All gameplay | Web Audio/offline signal tests; defaults/mute/end checks |\nEOF\ncat > docs/authoring.md <<'EOF'\n# Adding a maze\n\nAdd a version 1 stage object to src/content/stages.js. All stages use 21 × 17 rows of # walls and . floor; two hero spawns, twelve uniquely numbered f0–f11 foods (eight ordinary/four starred), three personality definitions inside the centred pen, paired horizontal tunnels, gate and reveal presets, introduction/clear copy, seed and stable ID. The existing authored corridor segment lists are editable data, not AI branches.\n\nKeep the 5 × 5 permanent pen at x8–12/y6–10, its 3 × 3 interior, four possible door cells, and an exterior connected ring. The door is a graph state, never a decorative-only wall. Set gate.turning to introduce rotations. Reveal kind is none, all, or bands; the latter fades only upper/lower sections. Predators have data-driven release times and speed multipliers.\n\nM.validate reports actionable errors and cells: dimensions/types, boundaries, paired tunnel rows, food identity/type counts, distinct spawns, permanent pen, three roles, safe two-exit pockets, all-orientation reachability and at least six interception loops. Do not bypass it. Test a new board with legal-intent Bot and ordinary lives/speed, then use actual controls and view its last-three-food phase.\n\nThe Maze workshop exports {format:\\\"mix-up-maze\\\",version:1,board:...}. Import uses the same validator and retains the existing maze on error. Saves use a versioned profile with three slots; native engine settings have their own versioned schema. Invalid/unavailable storage falls back to visit memory with a notice.\n\nCustom shapes/materials live in view/theatre.js and extend E.SHAPES/E.MATERIALS. Creatures derive from E.Blob; their authoritative states drive their look, feet, squash, mouths and tells. Audio data/instruments live in audio/sound.js. Neither art nor audio draws gameplay randomness.\n\nBuild with npm run build. Test with npm test; targeted iterations use node tools/test.mjs --unit, --browser, or --hub. Open the HTML beside the development directory directly. No runtime resource fetches or CDN dependencies are required.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
