{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '10718,10735p' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js && rg -n 'const clicked|function clicked' vendor/engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"  clear() { this._cards.length = 0; }\n  /** is a card up? (hold play while it is) */\n  get carding() { return this._cards.some(c => c.big); }\n  /** the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or\n   *  until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title' */\n  attract(dt) {\n    const I = this.game.input, o = this.o, P = this.game.players || [I], n = P.length, joined = n !== (this._n || 1); this._n = n;\n    if (P.some(q => q.anyPressed()) || joined || clicked(I)) { this._idle = 0; this.phase = 'title'; return 'title'; }   // (any player's input, or one joining)\n    this._idle += dt;\n    const next = this.phase === 'title' ? (this._idle >= o.idle ? 'demo' : null) : this.phase === 'demo' ? (this._idle >= o.demo ? 'scores' : null) : this._idle >= o.scores ? 'title' : null;\n    if (next) { this.phase = next; this._idle = 0; }\n    return this.phase;\n  }\n  /** the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does) */\n  wake() { this.phase = 'title'; this._idle = 0; }\n  /** the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores */\n  endDemo() { this.phase = 'scores'; this._idle = 0; }\n  /** a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys */\n10648:const clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/main.js')\ns=p.read_text().replace(\\\"markActivity(){this.front.wake();}\\\",\\\"markActivity(){this.front.wake();this.lastActivityClock=performance.now();}\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"if(this.front.attract(dt)==='demo')\\\", \\\"if(this.front.attract(dt)==='demo'||performance.now()-this.lastActivityClock>=10000)\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/browser.py')\ns=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index('                tp.evaluate(\\\"\\\"\\\"()=>{const cv=game.screen.canvas')\nend=s.index(\\\"                tp.screenshot(path=str(OUT/(name+'-play.png')))\\\",start)\ns=s[:start]+'''                cdp=touchctx.new_cdp_session(tp);point=tp.evaluate('({x:innerWidth*.28,y:innerHeight*.65})');held={'x':point['x']+60,'y':point['y'],'id':91}\n                cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchStart','touchPoints':[dict(point,id=91)]});cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchMove','touchPoints':[held]});tp.wait_for_timeout(300)\n                check(name+' invisible drag steering moves hero',tp.evaluate('mix.world.players[0].m.x>1.5&&game.input.lastDevice===\\\"touch\\\"'))\n                touch_id=tp.evaluate('mix.touch?.id')\n                tp.evaluate(\\\"game.debug.command('stage',{index:3});mix.world.phase='playing';game.settings.set('autoChirp',false);mix.world.players[0].chirp=0;mix.world.reveal=0;mix.intentCache[0].a=false;mix.lastHUD='';mix.hud()\\\")\n                tp.wait_for_timeout(60);button=tp.locator('.mix-chirp').bounding_box();second={'x':button['x']+button['width']/2,'y':button['y']+button['height']/2,'id':92}\n                cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchStart','touchPoints':[held,second]});cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchEnd','touchPoints':[held]});tp.wait_for_timeout(120)\n                check(name+' second finger chirps without losing steering contact',tp.evaluate('mix.touch?.id')==touch_id and tp.evaluate('mix.world.reveal>0'))\n                cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{'type':'touchCancel','touchPoints':[]});tp.wait_for_timeout(250)\n                check(name+' pointer cancellation clears movement',tp.evaluate('mix.touch===null&&mix.intentCache[0].d===-1'))\n''' +s[end:]\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/simulation.mjs')\ns=p.read_text().replace(\\\"test('invalid maze schemas\\\", \\\"test('displayed numeric and word seeds can be entered again',()=>{for(const seed of ['4242','green grin']){const a=M.generate(seed),b=M.generate(String(a.seed));assert.deepEqual(a.rows,b.rows);const w=new M.World({mode:'remix',seed}),v=new M.World({mode:'remix',seed:a.seed});assert.deepEqual(w.data,v.data);assert.equal(w.rng.state,v.rng.state);}});\\\\ntest('invalid maze schemas\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n| I02 | Moderate input | Expiring-input simulation test | Releasing a held direction could start one more edge inside its 150 ms buffer. | Neutral release clears same-direction desire; an already committed edge finishes exactly at its next centre. Passed. |\n| I03 | Major mechanics | Shortest-route / gate timing test | The original 6-cell outer ring took 1 second, making a timed 1.5-second pen ride pointless. | Added connected outer approach lanes to turning-pen boards; measured detour is 18 cells / 3 seconds versus a planned 1.5-second ride. All orientations and playthroughs passed. |\n| I04 | Moderate layout | TV screenshot and safe-area bounds check | The title footer extended below the display. | Reduced native title button minimum height while retaining TV text size. Safe-area check passed. |\n| I05 | Minor layout | TV screenshot | Native touch-start UI left an empty rounded control at the top centre. | Hid unused native touch controls and added one persistent Menu control that opens native Shell. |\n| I06 | Moderate lifecycle | Real ten-second idle browser check | Engine simulation time can lag wall time, stretching title idle beyond ten seconds. | Native Arcade idle is retained with a monotonic wall-clock deadline. Verification follows. |\n\nA test fixture that accidentally opened a connected cell was corrected to isolate a floor cell. Browser tests now wait for actual input ticks and disambiguate native/content Back buttons. These test-harness corrections are not counted as game issues. Seed roundtrip and seam coordinates were improved during source review and are covered by regression checks.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs --browser\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
