{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files vendor/engine vendor/hub -g 'LICENSE*' -g 'COPYING*' && cat project.json && cat build/reports/simulation.json | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"vendor/engine/LICENSE\n{\n  \"title\": \"K.C. Munchkin Mix-Up\",\n  \"base\": \"KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416\",\n  \"selection\": \"crypto.randomInt from 50 distinct private candidates\",\n  \"engine\": \"pending\",\n  \"hub\": \"pending\"\n}\n{\n  \"passed\": 34,\n  \"failed\": 0,\n  \"skipped\": 0,\n  \"failures\": [],\n  \"details\": {\n    \"shortcut\": {\n      \"outerCells\": 18,\n      \"outerSeconds\": 3,\n      \"timedRideSeconds\": 1.5\n    },\n    \"generation\": {\n      \"count\": 64,\n      \"fallbacks\": 0\n    },\n    \"packetBytes\": 441,\n    \"playthroughs\": [\n      {\n        \"seats\": 1,\n        \"time\": 272.30833333325,\n        \"lives\": 5,\n        \"score\": 120,\n        \"stages\": [\n          {\n            \"stage\": 0,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat vendor/engine/LICENSE\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('project.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());d['engine']='my-3D2dge 0.89.1, 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691';d['hub']='Protocol 1, client 1.4.0, 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869';p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('src/release.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());d['testingFeedback']=['9 unique game issues were found and fixed; test-fixture corrections were counted separately.','0 critical or game-breaking issues.','Legal-intent full campaigns and the dedicated-host latency/loss run, combined with the pen shortcut measurement.','Syntax-only checks: useful for parsing, but they cannot establish maze readability, interception or controller feel.'];d['engineFeedback']=[\n'Native shaded pixels, Blob squash/look/feet, procedural sound buses and the TV Shell gave the game a consistent base.',\n'Yes. I initially made the outer pen detour too short and rearmed an attract transition each input tick; route and runtime tests corrected both.',\n'The authoritative graph, moving-snack simulation, swept contacts, validated workshop and host-authoritative Hub adapter.',\n'Extending grid motion for expiring turns, immediate reversal and tunnel seams while keeping rendering and networking separate from the rules.',\n'No vendored engine changes. GraphMover subclasses the native mover; original art, mouth/antenna animation, UI and synthesis extend native systems.',\n'An official GridMover graph-edge adapter with tunnel transforms, expiring buffers and swept motion segments.'\n];d['promptFeedback']=[\n'The distinctive moving-food premise and concrete acceptance checks for a complete playable game.',\n'The first-player duration is a hypothesis; strong route-planning bots finish much faster, and human first-run timing is unknown.',\n'Keeping six stages, the editor, couch co-op, dedicated hosting, touch and final-file packaging consistent under one ruleset.',\n'Separate mandatory feature gates from pacing hypotheses and request measured timing ranges rather than an assumed first-run duration.'\n];p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('tools/build.mjs');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('const css = readFileSync', 'const license = readFileSync(path.join(root, \\\"vendor/engine/LICENSE\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\");\\\\nconst css = readFileSync');s=s.replace('<script>\"'${escape(engine)}</script>'\"', '<\"'!-- my-3D2dge license'\"\\\\n\"'${license}'\"\\\\n-->\\\\n<script>\"'${escape(engine)}</script>'\"');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > docs/balance.md <<'EOF'\n# Balance and measured pacing\n\nDefaults are 6 cells/s for heroes, 60% initial and 98% final snack speed (3.6 → 5.88 cells/s), 3.65 cells/s base predator travel plus bounded junction decisions, six-second bright food, a 1.5-second recovery warning, 2.6-second pen cadence, four-second chirp cooldown, 0.85-second shared damage grace and five team lives. A clear restores one life. The food curve is monotonic and no catch uses a speed boost, teleport, dash or forced food clear.\n\nThe first whole-campaign bot experiment finished in about two minutes because random food goals were too passive. Food now strongly prefers distance from nearby heroes while retaining a committed destination, no open-junction reversals and short visible turn tells. Interception became the useful choice. The last three get restrained trails and rings; the last target gets a slightly larger presentation silhouette, without a larger collision radius or reduced speed.\n\nThe initial pen looked useful but was not. Its outer approach was six cells / one second; a well-timed ride took about 1.5 seconds. Turning stages now have connected approach lanes around the machinery. The measured adjacent-door outer detour is eighteen cells / three seconds, versus a planned 1.5-second ride when entering near the warning. Waiting an entire cadence can still be slower: reading the timing matters. All four orientations preserve connectivity and closure defers over occupied crossings.\n\nAt seed 4242, legal route-planning bots with normal movement, normal lives and no assistance clear the full campaign in 272.31 seconds solo and 141.46 seconds co-op. They catch all 72 snacks through the real six transitions. Twenty generated remix seeds also clear under normal rules; all 64 generation samples validate without fallback. The detailed stage times and lives are in build/reports/simulation.json.\n\nA dedicated host with two legal-input clients under 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss cleared three stages with 36 catches and one hit in the measured run. All 213 sampled client states matched an actual retained host snapshot. All four gate orientations appeared. Snapshots peaked at 567 bytes in that run. The test driver plans its turns one junction ahead; planning only on arrival was too late for the simulated network. Local clients predict movement presentation only, then reconcile; food, hits and score always await the host.\n\nFirst-time human 12–18-minute pacing has not been measured. The observed bot times are not labelled as human play or a listening/device review. The standalone campaign is untimed. The Hub declares eight minutes as a conservative playing estimate and honestly reports partial progress on time-up; it never skips stages or manufactures a victory.\nEOF\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Verification evidence\n\nRun \"'`node tools/test.mjs` (or `npm test`) in this directory. It captures noisy child output and prints only failures and one passed/failed/skipped count. Targeted `--unit`, `--browser`, `--touch`, `--hub` and `--hub-live` checks use the same entry point. Reports are generated under build/reports/; screenshots under build/screenshots/.\n\nThe final aggregate result is recorded in build/reports/latest.json and PROGRESS.md. The suites are not FPS gates.\n\n- Simulation: expiring turn buffers, neutral release, immediate reversal, stick hysteresis, walls, explicit tunnel seams, swept swaps, twelve unique moving identities, monotonic acceleration, deterministic simultaneous co-op collection, pickup-before-hit ordering, bounded power/chain, warning and recharge, harmless returns, damage grace, affected-only respawn, final-bite clear and zero-life failure.\n- Content: all five authored layouts plus the generated campaign board in every gate orientation, measured useful shortcut, 64 reproducible seeds, twenty normal-rule remix catches, strict imported metadata/IDs, actionable corrupt/disconnected board errors, workshop undo/redo/save/reload/code/play, unavailable/corrupt persistence.\n- Lifecycle: two whole-campaign legal-intent traces (solo/co-op), six final-target catches each, normal lives and speed, actual final HTML campaign/results/retry, native settings persistence/reset, ten real idle seconds, repeated attract exits with consumed input and no record pollution, live developer sliders/reset and assisted-record exclusion.\n- Controls: real keyboard/mouse events, native hover focus, standard-map pad stubs, last-device labels and PS/Xbox selection, Create+Options reservation, controller loss, two independently assigned local pads, phone/tablet profiles with real multi-contact CDP input, chirp/menu while holding a steering contact, cancellation and touch workshop selection. WebKit receives a focused iPhone-profile boot/play pass.\n- Audio: OfflineAudioContext runs every game SFX through native synthesis and each formant voice vowel; finite samples, non-silent output and bounded peaks are checked. Native music/SFX/voice buses, the single 10% music gain, mute and synchronized pause are checked. There are no audio files in the bundle.\n- Hub: original official harness for one seat, two seats, impaired network, host leave and dedicated host. `window.__hubCheck.pass` must be true. A longer legal-input dedicated run checks actual collections, score/lives/gate/mask/revision and actor coordinates against retained authoritative packets, stage repair, sender/sequence rejection, local-menu continuity, missing heartbeat, player leave, tied co-op reporting, partial time-up, exactly-once finish and terminal silence/transport freeze.\n- Package: standalone file opening, no local/CDN resource requests, first-script byte-identical session client, strict metadata/interview shape and correct catalogue title. Pinned vendored repositories have no local changes. MIT permission text is embedded with the engine.\n\nPhysical DualSense/TV/phones/tablets/iOS, human listening quality and a first-time human campaign duration are unknown. Browser/device/controller stand-ins are explicitly used; these environmental limits are not silently counted as hardware passes. All owned browser contexts and temporary 127.0.0.1 servers close in finally blocks. No neighbouring processes or fixed ports are touched.\n\nNine unique issues are recorded in docs/issues.md. Test fixture mistakes (including asynchronous input waits and multi-contact CDP release IDs) are separate from game issue counts.\nEOF\ncat > tests/visual.py <<'\"'EOF'\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nR=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];P=json.loads((R/'project.json').read_text());URL=(R.parent/(P['base']+'.html')).as_uri()+'?test=1';O=R/'build/screenshots';O.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);passed=failed=0;failures=[]\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--no-sandbox'])\n try:\n  c=b.new_context(viewport={'width':1920,'height':1080});pg=c.new_page();pg.goto(URL);pg.wait_for_function('window.mix');pg.wait_for_timeout(400);pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-title-tv.png'));pg.get_by_role('button',name='Play solo',exact=True).click();pg.wait_for_function('mix.screen===\\\"play\\\"');pg.wait_for_timeout(2600)\n  pg.evaluate(\\\"game.debug.command('stage',{index:3});mix.world.god=true;mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.reveal=0;game.input.hold('right');game.advance(.5,{draw:true})\\\");pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'vanishing-tv.png'));pg.keyboard.press('Space');pg.wait_for_timeout(100);pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'revealed-tv.png'))\n  pg.evaluate(\\\"game.input.clear();game.debug.command('stage',{index:2});mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.gateTime=2.25;mix.world.stageTime=2;game.stop()\\\")\n  frames=[]\n  for i in range(7):\n   pg.evaluate('game.advance(.1,{draw:true})');name=O/f'gate-{i}.png';pg.screenshot(path=str(name));frames.append(str(name))\n  subprocess.run(['magick','montage',*frames,'-resize','480x270','-tile','7x1','-geometry','+4+4',str(O/'gate-motion-strip.png')],check=True,capture_output=True)\n  passed+=1;c.close()\n  c=b.new_context(**p.devices['iPhone 13']);pg=c.new_page();pg.goto(URL);pg.wait_for_function('window.mix');pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-title-phone.png'));pg.get_by_role('button',name='Play solo',exact=True).tap();pg.wait_for_function('mix.screen===\\\"play\\\"');pg.wait_for_timeout(2600);pg.evaluate(\\\"game.debug.command('stage',{index:3});mix.world.god=true;mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.reveal=0;game.input.lastDevice='touch';game.advance(.2,{draw:true})\\\");pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-play-phone.png'));passed+=1;c.close()\n except Exception as e:failed+=1;failures.append(str(e))\n finally:b.close()\nprint(json.dumps({'passed':passed,'failed':failed,'skipped':0,'failures':failures}))\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tools/test.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace('if (all || args.includes(\\\"--unit\\\"))', 'if(args.includes(\\\"--visual\\\"))run(\\\"visual\\\",\\\"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\\\",[\\\"tests/visual.py\\\"]);\\\\nif (all || args.includes(\\\"--unit\\\"))');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write src tools/*.mjs tests/simulation.mjs package.json project.json\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs --visual\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat vendor/engine/LICENSE\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('project.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());d['engine']='my-3D2dge 0.89.1, 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691';d['hub']='Protocol 1, client 1.4.0, 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869';p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('src/release.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());d['testingFeedback']=['9 unique game issues were found and fixed; test-fixture corrections were counted separately.','0 critical or game-breaking issues.','Legal-intent full campaigns and the dedicated-host latency/loss run, combined with the pen shortcut measurement.','Syntax-only checks: useful for parsing, but they cannot establish maze readability, interception or controller feel.'];d['engineFeedback']=[\n'Native shaded pixels, Blob squash/look/feet, procedural sound buses and the TV Shell gave the game a consistent base.',\n'Yes. I initially made the outer pen detour too short and rearmed an attract transition each input tick; route and runtime tests corrected both.',\n'The authoritative graph, moving-snack simulation, swept contacts, validated workshop and host-authoritative Hub adapter.',\n'Extending grid motion for expiring turns, immediate reversal and tunnel seams while keeping rendering and networking separate from the rules.',\n'No vendored engine changes. GraphMover subclasses the native mover; original art, mouth/antenna animation, UI and synthesis extend native systems.',\n'An official GridMover graph-edge adapter with tunnel transforms, expiring buffers and swept motion segments.'\n];d['promptFeedback']=[\n'The distinctive moving-food premise and concrete acceptance checks for a complete playable game.',\n'The first-player duration is a hypothesis; strong route-planning bots finish much faster, and human first-run timing is unknown.',\n'Keeping six stages, the editor, couch co-op, dedicated hosting, touch and final-file packaging consistent under one ruleset.',\n'Separate mandatory feature gates from pacing hypotheses and request measured timing ranges rather than an assumed first-run duration.'\n];p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('tools/build.mjs');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('const css = readFileSync', 'const license = readFileSync(path.join(root, \\\"vendor/engine/LICENSE\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\");\\\\nconst css = readFileSync');s=s.replace('<script>\"'${escape(engine)}</script>'\"', '<\"'!-- my-3D2dge license'\"\\\\n\"'${license}'\"\\\\n-->\\\\n<script>\"'${escape(engine)}</script>'\"');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > docs/balance.md <<'EOF'\n# Balance and measured pacing\n\nDefaults are 6 cells/s for heroes, 60% initial and 98% final snack speed (3.6 → 5.88 cells/s), 3.65 cells/s base predator travel plus bounded junction decisions, six-second bright food, a 1.5-second recovery warning, 2.6-second pen cadence, four-second chirp cooldown, 0.85-second shared damage grace and five team lives. A clear restores one life. The food curve is monotonic and no catch uses a speed boost, teleport, dash or forced food clear.\n\nThe first whole-campaign bot experiment finished in about two minutes because random food goals were too passive. Food now strongly prefers distance from nearby heroes while retaining a committed destination, no open-junction reversals and short visible turn tells. Interception became the useful choice. The last three get restrained trails and rings; the last target gets a slightly larger presentation silhouette, without a larger collision radius or reduced speed.\n\nThe initial pen looked useful but was not. Its outer approach was six cells / one second; a well-timed ride took about 1.5 seconds. Turning stages now have connected approach lanes around the machinery. The measured adjacent-door outer detour is eighteen cells / three seconds, versus a planned 1.5-second ride when entering near the warning. Waiting an entire cadence can still be slower: reading the timing matters. All four orientations preserve connectivity and closure defers over occupied crossings.\n\nAt seed 4242, legal route-planning bots with normal movement, normal lives and no assistance clear the full campaign in 272.31 seconds solo and 141.46 seconds co-op. They catch all 72 snacks through the real six transitions. Twenty generated remix seeds also clear under normal rules; all 64 generation samples validate without fallback. The detailed stage times and lives are in build/reports/simulation.json.\n\nA dedicated host with two legal-input clients under 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss cleared three stages with 36 catches and one hit in the measured run. All 213 sampled client states matched an actual retained host snapshot. All four gate orientations appeared. Snapshots peaked at 567 bytes in that run. The test driver plans its turns one junction ahead; planning only on arrival was too late for the simulated network. Local clients predict movement presentation only, then reconcile; food, hits and score always await the host.\n\nFirst-time human 12–18-minute pacing has not been measured. The observed bot times are not labelled as human play or a listening/device review. The standalone campaign is untimed. The Hub declares eight minutes as a conservative playing estimate and honestly reports partial progress on time-up; it never skips stages or manufactures a victory.\nEOF\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Verification evidence\n\nRun \"'`node tools/test.mjs` (or `npm test`) in this directory. It captures noisy child output and prints only failures and one passed/failed/skipped count. Targeted `--unit`, `--browser`, `--touch`, `--hub` and `--hub-live` checks use the same entry point. Reports are generated under build/reports/; screenshots under build/screenshots/.\n\nThe final aggregate result is recorded in build/reports/latest.json and PROGRESS.md. The suites are not FPS gates.\n\n- Simulation: expiring turn buffers, neutral release, immediate reversal, stick hysteresis, walls, explicit tunnel seams, swept swaps, twelve unique moving identities, monotonic acceleration, deterministic simultaneous co-op collection, pickup-before-hit ordering, bounded power/chain, warning and recharge, harmless returns, damage grace, affected-only respawn, final-bite clear and zero-life failure.\n- Content: all five authored layouts plus the generated campaign board in every gate orientation, measured useful shortcut, 64 reproducible seeds, twenty normal-rule remix catches, strict imported metadata/IDs, actionable corrupt/disconnected board errors, workshop undo/redo/save/reload/code/play, unavailable/corrupt persistence.\n- Lifecycle: two whole-campaign legal-intent traces (solo/co-op), six final-target catches each, normal lives and speed, actual final HTML campaign/results/retry, native settings persistence/reset, ten real idle seconds, repeated attract exits with consumed input and no record pollution, live developer sliders/reset and assisted-record exclusion.\n- Controls: real keyboard/mouse events, native hover focus, standard-map pad stubs, last-device labels and PS/Xbox selection, Create+Options reservation, controller loss, two independently assigned local pads, phone/tablet profiles with real multi-contact CDP input, chirp/menu while holding a steering contact, cancellation and touch workshop selection. WebKit receives a focused iPhone-profile boot/play pass.\n- Audio: OfflineAudioContext runs every game SFX through native synthesis and each formant voice vowel; finite samples, non-silent output and bounded peaks are checked. Native music/SFX/voice buses, the single 10% music gain, mute and synchronized pause are checked. There are no audio files in the bundle.\n- Hub: original official harness for one seat, two seats, impaired network, host leave and dedicated host. `window.__hubCheck.pass` must be true. A longer legal-input dedicated run checks actual collections, score/lives/gate/mask/revision and actor coordinates against retained authoritative packets, stage repair, sender/sequence rejection, local-menu continuity, missing heartbeat, player leave, tied co-op reporting, partial time-up, exactly-once finish and terminal silence/transport freeze.\n- Package: standalone file opening, no local/CDN resource requests, first-script byte-identical session client, strict metadata/interview shape and correct catalogue title. Pinned vendored repositories have no local changes. MIT permission text is embedded with the engine.\n\nPhysical DualSense/TV/phones/tablets/iOS, human listening quality and a first-time human campaign duration are unknown. Browser/device/controller stand-ins are explicitly used; these environmental limits are not silently counted as hardware passes. All owned browser contexts and temporary 127.0.0.1 servers close in finally blocks. No neighbouring processes or fixed ports are touched.\n\nNine unique issues are recorded in docs/issues.md. Test fixture mistakes (including asynchronous input waits and multi-contact CDP release IDs) are separate from game issue counts.\nEOF\ncat > tests/visual.py <<'\"'EOF'\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nR=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];P=json.loads((R/'project.json').read_text());URL=(R.parent/(P['base']+'.html')).as_uri()+'?test=1';O=R/'build/screenshots';O.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);passed=failed=0;failures=[]\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--no-sandbox'])\n try:\n  c=b.new_context(viewport={'width':1920,'height':1080});pg=c.new_page();pg.goto(URL);pg.wait_for_function('window.mix');pg.wait_for_timeout(400);pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-title-tv.png'));pg.get_by_role('button',name='Play solo',exact=True).click();pg.wait_for_function('mix.screen===\\\"play\\\"');pg.wait_for_timeout(2600)\n  pg.evaluate(\\\"game.debug.command('stage',{index:3});mix.world.god=true;mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.reveal=0;game.input.hold('right');game.advance(.5,{draw:true})\\\");pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'vanishing-tv.png'));pg.keyboard.press('Space');pg.wait_for_timeout(100);pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'revealed-tv.png'))\n  pg.evaluate(\\\"game.input.clear();game.debug.command('stage',{index:2});mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.gateTime=2.25;mix.world.stageTime=2;game.stop()\\\")\n  frames=[]\n  for i in range(7):\n   pg.evaluate('game.advance(.1,{draw:true})');name=O/f'gate-{i}.png';pg.screenshot(path=str(name));frames.append(str(name))\n  subprocess.run(['magick','montage',*frames,'-resize','480x270','-tile','7x1','-geometry','+4+4',str(O/'gate-motion-strip.png')],check=True,capture_output=True)\n  passed+=1;c.close()\n  c=b.new_context(**p.devices['iPhone 13']);pg=c.new_page();pg.goto(URL);pg.wait_for_function('window.mix');pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-title-phone.png'));pg.get_by_role('button',name='Play solo',exact=True).tap();pg.wait_for_function('mix.screen===\\\"play\\\"');pg.wait_for_timeout(2600);pg.evaluate(\\\"game.debug.command('stage',{index:3});mix.world.god=true;mix.world.phase='playing';mix.world.reveal=0;game.input.lastDevice='touch';game.advance(.2,{draw:true})\\\");pg.screenshot(path=str(O/'final-play-phone.png'));passed+=1;c.close()\n except Exception as e:failed+=1;failures.append(str(e))\n finally:b.close()\nprint(json.dumps({'passed':passed,'failed':failed,'skipped':0,'failures':failures}))\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('tools/test.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace('if (all || args.includes(\\\"--unit\\\"))', 'if(args.includes(\\\"--visual\\\"))run(\\\"visual\\\",\\\"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\\\",[\\\"tests/visual.py\\\"]);\\\\nif (all || args.includes(\\\"--unit\\\"))');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write src tools/*.mjs tests/simulation.mjs package.json project.json\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs --visual\"","aggregated_output":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Michael Crosato\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\nChecked 20 files in 32ms. Fixed 2 files.\nFAIL Command '['magick', 'montage', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-0.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-1.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-2.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-3.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-4.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-5.png', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-6.png', '-resize', '480x270', '-tile', '7x1', '-geometry', '+4+4', '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022416__xcf48cf/work/KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416/build/screenshots/gate-motion-strip.png']' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n0 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
