{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat tools/test.mjs && ls -lh ../*.html ../exit-interview.json && sed -n '1,70p' docs/issues.md\"","aggregated_output":"import { spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { root } from \"./load.mjs\";\n\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2),\n  all = args.length === 0 || args.includes(\"--all\");\nlet passed = 0,\n  failed = 0,\n  skipped = 0;\nconst reports = [];\nconst run = (name, command, argv) => {\n  const p = spawnSync(command, argv, { cwd: root, encoding: \"utf8\", maxBuffer: 12 * 1024 * 1024 });\n  let result;\n  try {\n    result = JSON.parse(p.stdout.trim());\n  } catch {\n    result = { passed: 0, failed: 1, skipped: 0, failures: [`${name}: ${p.stdout}\\n${p.stderr}`] };\n  }\n  passed += result.passed || 0;\n  failed += result.failed || 0;\n  skipped += result.skipped || 0;\n  reports.push({ name, ...result });\n  for (const f of result.failures || []) console.log(\"FAIL \" + f);\n  for (const s of result.limitations || []) console.log(\"SKIP \" + s);\n};\nif (args.includes(\"--visual\"))\n  run(\"visual\", \"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\", [\"tests/visual.py\"]);\nif (all || args.includes(\"--unit\")) run(\"simulation\", \"node\", [\"tests/simulation.mjs\"]);\nif (all || args.includes(\"--browser\") || args.includes(\"--smoke\"))\n  run(\"browser\", \"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\", [\n    \"tests/browser.py\",\n    ...(args.includes(\"--smoke\") ? [\"--smoke\"] : []),\n  ]);\nif (all || args.includes(\"--touch\"))\n  run(\"touch\", \"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\", [\"tests/touch.py\"]);\nif (args.includes(\"--hub-live\"))\n  run(\"hub-live\", \"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\", [\n    \"tests/hub.py\",\n    \"--live-only\",\n  ]);\nif (all || args.includes(\"--hub\"))\n  run(\"hub\", \"/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\", [\"tests/hub.py\"]);\nmkdirSync(path.join(root, \"build/reports\"), { recursive: true });\nwriteFileSync(\n  path.join(root, \"build/reports/latest.json\"),\n  JSON.stringify({ passed, failed, skipped, reports }, null, 2) + \"\\n\",\n);\nconsole.log(`${passed} passed, ${failed} failed, ${skipped} skipped`);\nprocess.exitCode = failed ? 1 : 0;\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1.4M Nov  6 03:37 ../KC-Munchkin-Mix-Up-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022416.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 3.7K Nov  6 03:37 ../exit-interview.json\n# Issue ledger\n\nOnly unique issues found by verification count here. Counts are finalized after release checks.\n\n| ID | Severity | Caught by | Finding | Fix / verification |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I01 | Major balance | First legal-input campaign trace | Snacks followed random goals too passively; the full solo campaign cleared in 120 seconds and many boards ended before feature exploration. | Strengthened committed fleeing at junctions, retained no-reversal policy and small turn tells; legal traces now take longer and use route cuts. Broader timing samples pending. |\n\nFocused code review also corrected seam reversal coordinate representation and numeric seed re-hashing before the browser/net suites; these are recorded design corrections, not extra claimed testing findings.\n| I02 | Moderate input | Expiring-input simulation test | Releasing a held direction could start one more edge inside its 150 ms buffer. | Neutral release clears same-direction desire; an already committed edge finishes exactly at its next centre. Passed. |\n| I03 | Major mechanics | Shortest-route / gate timing test | The original 6-cell outer ring took 1 second, making a timed 1.5-second pen ride pointless. | Added connected outer approach lanes to turning-pen boards; measured detour is 18 cells / 3 seconds versus a planned 1.5-second ride. All orientations and playthroughs passed. |\n| I04 | Moderate layout | TV screenshot and safe-area bounds check | The title footer extended below the display. | Reduced native title button minimum height while retaining TV text size. Safe-area check passed. |\n| I05 | Minor layout | TV screenshot | Native touch-start UI left an empty rounded control at the top centre. | Hid unused native touch controls and added one persistent Menu control that opens native Shell. |\n| I06 | Moderate lifecycle | Real ten-second idle browser check | The title input hook rearmed its transition fade every tick once idle elapsed; simulation-time idle could also lag the real deadline. | Attract entry uses a single cut on the next fixed step, and native Arcade idle has a monotonic wall-clock deadline. Verification follows. |\n\nA test fixture that accidentally opened a connected cell was corrected to isolate a floor cell. Browser tests now wait for actual input ticks and disambiguate native/content Back buttons. These test-harness corrections are not counted as game issues. Seed roundtrip and seam coordinates were improved during source review and are covered by regression checks.\n| I07 | Moderate touch | Phone/tablet multitouch browser checks | A non-primary finger did not reliably create a click on the contextual chirp button. | Gameplay HUD actions now trigger on touch pointer-down while preserving the existing steering contact; duplicate compatibility clicks are consumed. |\n| I08 | Moderate editor | Touch tool-palette scenario | Opening a palette on pointer-down could click through to its first new item on release. | Consume the initiating compatibility click at the window capture boundary; a new contact still selects normally. |\n| I09 | Moderate editor | Touch palette / return-to-editor scenario | Closing a custom workshop overlay could leave the native game paused without a visible overlay. | Workshop close explicitly restores simulation/editor input; native pause/developer back navigation remains native. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
