{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/main.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('        this.sound.unlock();\\\\n        if (this.screen === \\\"attract\\\") {', '''        if(e.type===\\\"keydown\\\")this.game.input.lastDevice=\\\"keyboard\\\";\n        if(e.type===\\\"pointerdown\\\")this.game.input.lastDevice=e.pointerType===\\\"touch\\\"?\\\"touch\\\":\\\"mouse\\\";\n        if(e.type===\\\"pointermove\\\")this.game.input.lastDevice=\\\"mouse\\\";\n        if(e.type===\\\"keydown\\\"||e.type===\\\"pointerdown\\\")this.sound.unlock();\n        this.lastHUD=\\\"\\\";\n        if (this.screen === \\\"attract\\\") {''')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/hub.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"const motion=win.mix.net.predicted||hero.m;if(motion.moving){const to=motion._to,edge=host.mix.world.revision+':'+motion.cx+','+motion.cy+'>'+to.join(',');\\\", \\\"const motion=hero.m;if(motion.moving){const to=motion._to,edge=host.mix.world.revision+':'+motion.cx+','+motion.cy+'>'+to.join(',');\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/browser.py');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"page.get_by_role('button',name='How to play',exact=True).hover()\\\", \\\"page.get_by_role('button',name='How to play',exact=True).hover()\\\\n        check('pointer hover does not unlock audio before a user gesture',page.evaluate('\"'!mix.sound.unlocked&&!game.audio.ctx'\"'))\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/rules.md');s=p.read_text().replace('stale authenticated intents expire after 650 ms.', 'stale authenticated intents expire after 650 ms. Direction/action changes are reliable; small unreliable heartbeats repair held state. Failed sends retain at most the current input/action intent for bounded retry.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write src tools/*.mjs tests/simulation.mjs package.json project.json\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnpm test\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > docs/visual-review.md <<'EOF'\n# Visual review\n\nInspected rendered images rather than using screenshots as gameplay proof. Legal play and protocol evidence are separate tests.\n\n- TV at 1920 × 1080: the complete board fits inside its cabinet surround; the native focus ring, six title actions, footer and score/life/remaining-food hierarchy are legible. Hero rings and numbers remain visible. The title footer was shortened into the safe area; an inactive toast is explicitly hidden.\n- Creature distinction: cool round antenna heroes, small warm edible faces, starred power snacks, narrow Needle, pointed-eared Peek and broad Chonk read differently. Co-op uses different head details as well as colour and numbered rings.\n- Phone portrait: the whole board fits the width with no joystick graphic. Menu stays clear of the stage label. Contextual chirp lives below the board and shows cooldown. Touch editor selection has a compact palette and real tools.\n- Vanishing stage: boundary and pen stay visible while inner wall bodies fade. Faint landmarks and the nearby collision echo preserve orientation. The chirp restores the actual walls; it does not reveal a different collision map.\n- Gate motion strip: the wind-up cue precedes the door change, the opening moves a quarter turn, and the rotor settles. The one active opening always matches the graph; no simultaneous opposite doors are drawn.\n- Results, credits and workshop use the native TV Shell and its focus/scroll behaviour. Feedback is paginated rather than squeezed into one panel.\n\nRepresentative files: build/screenshots/title-tv.png, play-tv.png, victory-tv.png, coop-tv.png, workshop-tv.png, credits-tv.png, final-title-phone.png, final-play-phone.png, vanishing-tv.png, revealed-tv.png and gate-motion-strip.png. These are browser/device-profile stand-ins. Physical television, phone, tablet and controller verification is unknown.\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Release-candidate checks\n- Full suite passed once: **155 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** on the bundled game. This included normal whole campaigns, final-file campaign/retry, all browser/device/credits/workshop checks, 16 touch checks, five official Hub scenarios and the longer dedicated gameplay case.\n- Visual review completed for TV, phone, disappearing/revealed walls and a seven-frame gate motion strip. An inactive toast needed an explicit hidden style after its position was customized. HUD buttons now hide correctly beneath pause overlays.\n- Final minor refinements: real gestures (not pointer hover) unlock audio; DOM menu touch/mouse updates last-device prompts; directional/action changes are sent reliably with bounded current-intent retry; heartbeats remain small/unreliable. Hidden clients send neutral intent.\n- Final full suite is running again on that exact release candidate: session **93561**, \"'`npm test` (now quiet via local .npmrc). Do not change source while it runs unless a genuine failure requires it.\n- Final release metadata is filled in src/release.json and emitted identically to the root exit-interview.json and in-game About. Nine unique fixed issues, zero critical. Engine/Hub repos remain unmodified; MIT permission text is embedded in HTML.\n- project.json moved into the development directory; all build/tests now read it there. Root contains PLAN.md, TASK.md, PROGRESS.md, the final HTML and exit-interview.json.\n- Remaining: inspect final results and current TV/co-op image, validate schema/deterministic build without rewriting it, update final counts/docs, confirm owned browser/server teardown, and deliver the mandated source/feedback text with links.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=Path('src/release.json');d=json.loads(r.read_text());s=d['sourceInformation'];lines=['# Release handoff','',f\\\"Game: {d['aiHub']['name']}\\\",'','Source Information','']\nfor k,v in s.items():lines.append(f'- {k}: {v}')\nfor title,key in [('Testing Feedback','testingFeedback'),('Engine Feedback','engineFeedback'),('Prompt Feedback','promptFeedback')]:\n lines+=['',title,'']+[f'{i+1}. {a}' for i,a in enumerate(d[key])]\nPath('docs/handoff.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Release schema:',list(d),'feedback lengths:',[len(d[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
